  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/106",
    "id": 5104070648,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABMDnv-A",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/106",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/106.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/106.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/106",
    "number": 106,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "docs(ctx-auth-002): close CTX-AUTH-002 (qualified); ADR-KERNEL-08 IMPLEMENTED",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "## Closes CTX-AUTH-002 (qualified) and moves ADR-KERNEL-08 to IMPLEMENTED (documentation only)\n\nPR #93 is merged (`b742e4a`) and re-verified on `main`. This records the resulting statuses, and only those the documents' own terms support.\n\n### Why this is justified\nCTX-AUTH-002's own status text named exactly two reasons it wasn't closed: the replacement was \"**not promoted to `main` and not re-verified there**. Nothing here is a closure.\" ADR-KERNEL-08 §8.1 item 4 says the ADR moves to IMPLEMENTED \"after promotion and re-verification on `main`\". Both are now true:\n\n| Re-verification on merged `main` | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Merged tree vs tested head `396e374` | identical |\n| Suite | 2176 passed, 1 xfailed, 8 failed. Pre-merge `main`: 2087 / 1 / 8. **The same 8** `tests/core/sandbox/test_namespace_backend.py` environment failures (no namespace privileges in my sandbox; CI runs them green) |\n| Drift / mutation | 30 PASS, 0 FAIL / 43/43 caught, sources byte-identical |\n| Six dry-run stand-ins, 10x3 | all exit 0, ESCALATED 0 (scripted, not real-model evidence) |\n| CI on the merge commit | `tests`, `drift-and-ownership`, CodeQL analyses all success |\n| Harness hash on `main` | equals the one recorded by the owner's real run |\n\n### What \"closed\" means here, and what it does not\n**Closed (qualified):** the tested authority/escalation path, verified mechanically on the corpus and mutations tested, plus the owner's real-model run (`llama3`, 120 exposed adversarial trials, **ESCALATED 0**, 2 advisory selections).\n**Not claimed:** \"proved with a real LLM\"; that real hostile exploitation is impossible; anything beyond one model, one sample, four payloads. Residuals R1-R6 stand (R3 measured: 33% benign fallback to `novel`, the cost judgement is the owner's; R5 has one real data point, not closure).\n\n### Explicitly NOT closed\n- **CTX-AUTH-001b stays OPEN.** ADR §8.1 item 4 only says it \"may be reconsidered\"; that is a separate owner decision I have not made.\n- REM-004 is not closed. DEBT-025 and everything else untouched. ADR-KERNEL-08 is IMPLEMENTED, **not FINAL**.\n\n### What changed\nADR-KERNEL-08 header, §8.2 item 4 and §9 (**§§1-8.1, the approved text, are byte-identical**, checked by diff, 330 lines); `ADR_INDEX.md`; the threat model's CTX-AUTH-002 status (and a dated note on CTX-AUTH-001b, classification untouched); the remediation register; `CURRENT_STATE.md`; `KNOWN_ISSUES.md`, including the DEBT-019 row that still said the harness review and real-provider run were \"outstanding\". Historical sync entries are kept as \"Prior sync\".\n",
    "created_at": "2026-11-01T03:39:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-01T12:31:28Z",
