  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/104",
    "id": 5096241623,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABL8J51w",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/104",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/104.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/104.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/104",
    "number": 104,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "fix(fz02-b2c): close the provider stream and leak no tasks when the router's caller task is cancelled",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "## FZ-02 batch B2c (narrowed): router-level resource cleanup when the caller task is cancelled\n\n### Owner sign-off (2026-10-31), narrow, on the exact head `4891756b4864c15c4e8df534560a46f5ce7fe34c`\nSigned off by the repo owner in chat as a **resource-cleanup fix only**. The sign-off is recorded here by Claude from that instruction. Boundaries, stated explicitly:\n1. **Guaranteed:** when the task running the provider call is cancelled, the router stops its consumer/watchdog tasks and the provider stream closes (no task outlives the request), and a caller cancellation arriving during the router's own consumer cancellation is not swallowed.\n2. **Not done:** this does **not** make the graph watchdog cancel node tasks. It only sets a token that nothing in the node observes.\n3. **Not established:** this does **not** establish that execution stops on cancellation. Successful cleanup must not be read as successful cancellation of the workflow.\n4. **Unverified:** shutdown, Ctrl-C and client-disconnect cancellation; physical provider-side termination.\n5. **Tracked separately:** `Worker.execute()` converts task cancellation into a failed result and the workflow retries (`core/workers/base.py:293`): **#105**, unassigned, needs its own owner, branch, tests and an explicit decision on the cancellation contract. It is not fixed or decided here.\n6. **Deferred, unreviewed:** token-driven cancellation, on `follow-up/fz02-b2d-latent-token-cancellation-oct2026`.\n**Merging this PR does not close the broader cancellation gap and does not mark workflow cancellation as solved.** FZ-01 stays open; no freeze claim follows.\n\n**Owner decision (2026-10-31):** keep only the production-reachable behaviour in this PR; defer the token-driven portion until a production caller threads a cancellation token. The deferred work is preserved, not discarded: branch `follow-up/fz02-b2d-latent-token-cancellation-oct2026` (no PR, not reviewed; record in `docs/handoffs/fz02_b2d_latent_token_cancellation.md`).\n\n**Review target (base):** `main` @ `16d663a`. **Head:** `4891756` = `fc845d0` (the first, un-narrowed B2c commit) + one additive narrowing commit; no history was rewritten. The net diff against `main` is two files.\n\n### Change (`core/model_router.py` only, +34/-5)\n- When the **caller task** is cancelled while the router waits, it now stops its consumer and watchdog tasks and waits for them, so the provider stream's `finally` runs and no task outlives the request, then re-raises its own `CancelledError`.\n- A caller cancellation arriving while the router is cancelling its own consumer is no longer swallowed (`await consumer_task` under `except CancelledError: pass` was replaced by `asyncio.wait({consumer_task})` + `.result()`).\n- `AdapterRuntime` is unchanged: it already lets `CancelledError` propagate (no fallback, no health penalty); this is now pinned by tests. Genuine failures and genuine stalls keep their behaviour (pinned).\n\nNot in this PR: `FailureType.CANCELLED` classification, the CANCELLED training-pair guard, the `AdapterRuntime` pre-attempt token check and terminal `cancelled` handling, `is_caller_cancellation()`, the two strict xfails. All of them are in the follow-up branch with their tests.\n\n### Production reachability (verified)\n- No production caller gives the router or `AdapterRuntime` a token: `PlannerWorker` (`planner.py:321-345`) passes `context_memory` (no `cancellation_token`), `capability_executor.py:116` passes `\"\"`, `orchestrator.py:923` passes `context_memory`. `_request_token()` returns `None` for both request shapes; `_resolve_cancellation_token()` returns a fresh local token each call. That is why token-driven cancellation is deferred.\n- **The graph watchdog does not stop a node's task.** `GraphExecutionWatchdog` only sets the workflow token; it is read cooperatively between nodes / before retries (`workflow/runtime.py:723,865`), and the planner node does not forward it to the router. Probe (`docs/handoffs/fz02_gate_probe.py` on the follow-up branch): graph budget hard=0.3 s, token cancelled with `execution hard_deadline`, the node nevertheless ran until the router's own hard deadline (workflow returned after 2.03 s). So the graph watchdog does **not** exercise this PR's behaviour.\n- This PR's behaviour is exercised only when something **cancels the task** that runs the workflow/node. In-process I found no such site on the request path (no `wait_for`/timeout around `handle()` or node execution; the `wait_for` in `safe_llm_call` wraps provider-mesh/evaluator calls, not the monitored-streaming path). External triggers (shutdown, Ctrl-C, client disconnect) were **not** verified. With a real `WorkflowRuntime` and the task cancelled at 0.5 s: the provider stream closes at 0.5 s with this change; on `main` no close is observed for that attempt.\n- **New finding, out of scope, not fixed here:** `Worker.execute()` (`core/workers/base.py:293`) converts `CancelledError` into `WorkerResult(success=False, error=\"Worker cancelled\")`. In the same probe `execute()` therefore **returned a result** (`task.cancelled()` is False) and the node was **retried** (attempts=2). A task cancel does not terminate a workflow today; this PR only guarantees the router cleans up and does not swallow it. Needs its own tracked item and owner decision.\n\n### Evidence (author's sandbox, Python 3.12, no chromadb; CI may differ)\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `tests/test_b2c_cancellation.py` on this head | 7 passed |\n| same tests on unchanged `main` | 3 failed (the fixes: stream/tasks cleanup, swallowed cancel, concurrent request), 4 passed (pins of unchanged behaviour) |\n| entire suite, `main` (before) | 8 failed / 2064 passed / 4 skipped / 1 xfailed / 4 collection errors |\n| entire suite, this head | 8 failed / 2071 passed / 4 skipped / 1 xfailed / 4 collection errors |\n| failing/erroring ids | identical set (12 ids, environmental) |\n| `scripts/check_drift.py`; `git diff --check`; CR bytes | rc 0; clean; 0 |\n\nCI on this exact head `4891756`: `tests`, `drift-and-ownership`, `CodeQL`, `Analyze (python)`, `Analyze (actions)` all completed with success.\n\n### Limitations (not claimed as fixed)\n1. **Physical provider-side termination on cancel is UNVERIFIED.** Only in-process stop is proven, with fakes.\n2. `Worker.execute()` swallows task cancellation above the router (new finding above; tracked as #105).\n3. A genuine failure or stall still benches `ModelRouterAdapter` and can start a second full generation on `OllamaAdapter` (B2a/B2b effects unchanged).\n4. Training pairs / `query_count` / promotion are still recorded for provider-failure, stalled and hard-deadline outcomes (tracked separately).\n5. `OllamaAdapter` error text can carry raw exception text (log-only today). `OpenAICompatAdapter`'s failure path is untested here. FZ-01 stays open; no freeze claim.\n\n### Impact\nGovernance: none (cancellation only stops work). Replay/observability: no new events. Security: no new disclosure. Compatibility: additive. Rollback: revert one file.\n\n### Process\nSingle owner, single branch. Signed off on the exact head (see above). `main` had not moved from `16d663a`, so no update-from-main was needed; merge with a merge commit pinned to the signed-off head, all five checks green. If `tests` fails with the ChromaDB native crash (exit 132), rerun only the failed job and record it as environmental.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-10-31T09:16:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-31T15:29:19Z",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-31T15:29:19Z",
    "merged_at": "2026-10-31T15:29:19Z",
    "merge_commit_sha": "ed3d141e4bbfd0231afb1104d0a7479419f9bbf1",
