    "body": "## DEBT-014 — final deep-review hardening for DRIFT-10\n\n**Base:** `main` at `7bb0ce2fd4b9557e56258f66d9f3e6b0e7bdca68`. This is a clean review branch; the previously closed PR #99 remains closed and unmerged.\n\n### What changed\n- Extend DRIFT-10 to inspect `core/cognitive/learning.py` with a structurally scoped exception for ValidationGate's required GovernanceKernel evaluation.\n- Fail closed on missing, non-regular, symlinked, unreadable, undecodable, or syntactically invalid governed files.\n- Detect module-scope bindings and nested `global` mutations; avoid false positives for attribute/subscript references, comprehension-local names, read-only globals, and annotation-only declarations.\n- Require the exact governance evaluation statement, terminal handling of ESCALATE/REJECT/non-APPROVE verdicts, preservation of the evaluated result, and constrained memory-write paths.\n- Reject writes or escapes of the result object, including attribute/subscript mutation, aliases, calls receiving the object, and common literal-reflection persistence-write aliases.\n- Make the runtime ValidationGate reject an unknown/future governance verdict rather than falling through to promotion.\n- Add adversarial static and runtime regression coverage. The shared environmental-failure allowlist is byte-for-byte unchanged from base.\n\n### Scope and limitations\n`KNOWN_ISSUES.md` is not modified; DEBT-014 remains OPEN pending owner acceptance and merge. DRIFT-10 is bounded AST analysis, not a proof against arbitrary dynamic execution (`exec`, computed reflection keys, custom proxy behavior, etc.) or every possible semantic/control-flow trick. These limitations are recorded rather than presented as solved.\n\n### Review request\nPlease inspect the exact PR head and new adversarial tests carefully. Do not merge automatically; owner decision remains required.",
