    "body": "## DEBT-014 — final review candidate: DRIFT-10 governance boundary\n\n**Review base:** `main` at `7bb0ce2fd4b9557e56258f66d9f3e6b0e7bdca68`.\n**Candidate source snapshot:** `0a9a67d2ef85e218872686fd472bb2a818b22821`.\n\n### Changes\n- Extend DRIFT-10 to inspect Intent, Planner, and Learning, with only the configured ValidationGate governance call allowed.\n- Add module-scope rebinding analysis for assignment/deletion, destructuring, loop and context-manager targets, exception aliases, assignment expressions, pattern captures, imports/star imports, and explicit global mutations.\n- Add context-aware target checks to avoid confusing attribute/subscript references with actual rebinding.\n- Require the exact direct governance call plus terminal ESCALATE, REJECT, and non-APPROVE guards; constrain the result binding and memory-write placement/count.\n- Make Evolution ValidationGate reject an unknown/future verdict rather than allowing it to fall through into promotion.\n- Harden governed-file path/symlink/read/decode/syntax validation and narrow symlink-test skips.\n- Keep `docs/architecture/D10_KNOWN_ENVIRONMENTAL_FAILURES.txt` byte-for-byte identical to the base. The prior seccomp allowlist expansion is not present.\n\n### Verification on this exact source commit\n- CI run #392: 2,150 passed, 14 skipped, 1 xfailed, 2 warnings; pytest exit code 0; test gate passed.\n- Architecture drift/ownership check: passed.\n- CodeQL Python and Actions analyses: passed.\n\n### Explicit limitation for independent review\nThis is bounded AST analysis, not a proof against arbitrary dynamic behavior or hidden helper side effects. In particular, please challenge scope rebinding variants (including a `global result` declaration inside the approved gate), aliased/dynamic persistence operations, and control-flow tricks that a direct-shape check may not fully model. Do not treat a clean structural check as proof of semantic equivalence; use the runtime regression tests as a second line of evidence.\n\n### Governance / merge state\n`KNOWN_ISSUES.md` is intentionally unchanged because concurrent work touches the register. DEBT-014 remains OPEN until independent review and owner-authorized merge. This PR is a stable handoff target and must not be merged automatically.",
    "created_at": "2026-10-29T14:41:25Z",
