    "body": "## DEBT-014 — harden the DRIFT-10 Learning governance boundary\n\n**Base:** `main` at `7bb0ce2fd4b9557e56258f66d9f3e6b0e7bdca68`.\n\n### Enforcement changes\n- Extend DRIFT-10 to scan `core/cognitive/learning.py` alongside Intent and Planner while allowing only the configured, structurally scoped ValidationGate governance call.\n- Detect module-scope rebinding forms: direct/destructuring assignments, deletion, loop and context-manager targets, exception aliases, assignment expressions, pattern captures, imports/star imports, and writes through nested `global` declarations.\n- Avoid false positives for attribute/subscript references, comprehension-local targets, read-only `global` declarations, and annotation-only declarations without values.\n- Require the exact `result = governance.evaluate_action(action)` call and terminal handling of `ESCALATE`, `REJECT`, and every non-`APPROVE` verdict before promotion. Exception reporting is emitted only when the complete result-flow contract passes.\n- Fail closed on governed-file path/symlink/read/decoding/syntax problems and narrow symlink-test skips to recognized platform/filesystem limitations.\n- Harden the runtime ValidationGate to reject unexpected/future governance verdicts rather than letting an unknown verdict fall through to promotion.\n\n### Regression coverage\nAdversarial AST tests cover missing rebinding forms, false-positive target patterns, nested global mutations, verdict-result bypasses, missing terminal verdict guards, filesystem failures, and skip behavior. Runtime coverage verifies an unrecognized governance verdict causes no memory write or event emission.\n\n### Scope and limitations\nNo changes to Intent/Planner runtime behavior. `docs/architecture/D10_KNOWN_ENVIRONMENTAL_FAILURES.txt` is byte-for-byte unchanged from the base. `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` is intentionally not edited because concurrent PRs also touch the register; DEBT-014 remains OPEN until the final review and owner-authorized merge.\n\nDRIFT-10 is deliberately a bounded AST structural check, not proof against arbitrary dynamic mutation (for example, `exec`/direct globals-dictionary manipulation), indirection, or all semantic control-flow tricks. The runtime regression test covers the specific unknown-verdict fail-open case addressed here.\n\n### Review status\nPR #99 is the canonical review target. PR #98 was closed as superseded; neither PR has been merged by this work. CI and CodeQL results for the final head are available in the PR checks.",
