    "body": "## DEBT-014 — close the DRIFT-10 governance-check coverage gap\n\n**Base:** `main` at `7bb0ce2fd4b9557e56258f66d9f3e6b0e7bdca68` (verified immediately before branching).\n\n### Change\n- Extend DRIFT-10's checked files to include `core/cognitive/learning.py`.\n- Preserve the legitimate Evolution-tier approval call in the module-level `validation_gate()` as a narrowly scoped structural exception: it must be the direct RHS of `result = governance.evaluate_action(action)`, with no keywords.\n- Report calls elsewhere in `learning.py`, extra calls within `validation_gate()`, nested functions or methods with the same name, wrapped expressions (including lambdas), or a changed call shape as violations.\n- Leave DRIFT-05 unchanged; it continues to cover `SupervisorWorker`.\n\n### Tests added\nSix synthetic-source tests cover an unauthorized call in another Learning function, the exact accepted exception, duplicate calls inside the exception scope, a changed call shape, a nested look-alike `validation_gate()`, and a wrapped/lambda call. Existing DRIFT-10 fixtures now include the third checked file.\n\n### Scope / status\nNo production runtime behavior changes. `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` is intentionally not edited because active PRs #91 and #97 also modify the register; DEBT-014 remains OPEN until exact-head checks pass and the register can be reconciled without overwriting concurrent debt updates.\n\n### Validation\nThe patch was built from current-main file blobs and passed source-anchor/shape checks. A local pytest run was not available in this session. CI and independent review must verify the final PR head; do not treat the debt as closed based on this PR alone.\n",
