  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/96",
    "id": 5066576474,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABLf3SWg",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/96",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/96.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/96.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/96",
    "number": 96,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "docs(register): resolve DEBT-044 on independent review; record the corrected operational consequence",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "## Resolves DEBT-044 (documentation only)\n\nDEBT-044's row said to keep it OPEN until independent review accepts the implementation. The owner supplied a source-level review of `main` `4a4783c`: **PASS, recommends closure**. This PR records that and closes the row. No code change.\n\n### What I re-checked rather than inherited\nThe review did not rerun the suite and submitted no formal GitHub review, so I re-verified its load-bearing claims against merged `main`: its test-group mapping (A,H,I / B-E / F / G,K / J) and every cited line reference hold; atomicity and retry behavior were reproduced independently of the PR's own tests (a failed `save()` leaks a half-written turn and entity into the next commit on `f13bfde`, and does not on `main`; DEBT-029's measurements cover retry).\n\n### One place where I do NOT follow the review\nIts \"residual behavior\" paragraph says that after a rollback failure the request handlers \"continue returning completed answers\". **Measured, that is only true of the request that hit the failure.** With the real `ContextMemory` driven into the disabled state by the PR's own Test I technique, then real requests through the real `ModelRouter` and `PlannerWorker` (only model generation stubbed):\n\n- `ModelRouter.route()` raises `ProgrammingError` while building the prompt, before any model call (`_build_prompt()` is the only reader of `format_for_prompt()` and is unguarded).\n- `PlannerWorker._run()` returns `success=True` with `[Error in knowledge: ProgrammingError (ref ...)]` as the answer, until the process restarts.\n\nSo the fail-closed read side costs answer availability, not only history availability. The trigger is narrow (rollback itself must fail) and the failure is loud and log-correlated, but it is an availability exposure. The row records it as measured, per the review's own advice to record it as a known operational consequence instead of holding the debt open.\n\n### Decision left to the owner\nIsolating the read side (degrade to a history-free prompt) or adding a bounded reconnect would reverse the fail-closed read behavior that `test_i_rollback_failure_disables_reads_and_writes_and_redacts` pins. I did not change it.\n\n### Also\n- DEBT-029's row said DEBT-044 \"stays OPEN pending its own independent review\"; updated so the live register doesn't contradict itself. The earlier dated sync entry is left as history.\n- DEBT-015 sub-item (7) and D-3 stay open.\n\nValidation: `check_drift.py` exit 0, no FAIL; the DEBT-044 and DEBT-029 test files pass (15); the full suite runs in CI.\n",
