    "body": "## Resolves DEBT-029\n\nDEBT-029 was left open by #89 with the note that whether the Step 8 guard satisfies its narrow fix was \"a separate decision\". The owner decided it must be satisfied. This PR re-verifies that against merged `main`, closes the register entry with evidence, and fixes the one same-class gap found along the way.\n\n### Evidence that the Step 8 guard satisfies DEBT-029\nScenario: real `WorkflowRuntime`, `RetryPolicy(max_retries=2)`, one counted capability call, `ContextMemory.save()` failing after it.\n\n| Code state | workflow | capability calls | save attempts | committed Test F |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| pre-fix `f13bfde` | failed | **3** | 3 | fails |\n| `f13bfde` + only the `planner.py` guard (D-5's own fix) | succeeded | **1** | 1 | passes |\n| merged `main` `6e41187` | succeeded | **1** | 1 | passes |\n| `main` with only `planner.py` reverted | failed | **3** | 3 | fails |\n\nThe Step 8 guard is the load-bearing change; DEBT-044's `ContextMemory` transaction safety does not by itself close DEBT-029.\n\n### Same-class gap found and fixed\nAfter the capability calls, the only other post-dispatch step that could raise was `merger.merge()`'s three-or-more-module branch. It is **reachable in production**: `classifier_v3.classify()` ignores `top_k` on its embedding path (only the keyword fallback caps at two). `_weave()` caught generation failures, but `resolve_provider(\"merger\")` ran outside its `try`. It now runs inside, and the fallback logs its exception type (type only, never the text). New `tests/test_debt_029_post_dispatch_merge_isolation.py`: 3 tests, the 2 provider-resolution cases fail on pre-change code (including an end-to-end `PlannerWorker._run()` case with the real merger).\n\n### Verification\n- Full suite: 2079 passed, 1 xfailed, 8 failed. The 8 are the `tests/core/sandbox/test_namespace_backend.py` namespace tests, which need privileges my sandbox lacks and fail identically on pristine `main`.\n- `scripts/check_drift.py`: exit 0, no FAIL.\n\n### Not changed / residual\n- DEBT-044 stays OPEN pending independent review.\n- Retry/idempotency semantics for side-effecting capabilities remain DEBT-015 sub-item (7); the crash+`resume()` variant (D-3) stands as recorded.\n- Observation only: `classify()`'s docstring says top-k but the embedding path never applies it. Not changed here; the owner's call.\n- Pre-existing, untouched: the DEBT-029 table row has DEBT-022's \"Resolved\" paragraph glued to the end of its line.\n",
