    "number": 93,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "CTX-AUTH-002: reconcile approved remediation with main (ADR-KERNEL-08, harness remediation)",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "## What this is\n\nPromotes the approved CTX-AUTH-002 remediation line to a reviewable PR, reconciled against current `main`.\n\n- **Base:** `main` at `6e411877e426646f3c40892c75f407991b4d235b` (PR #89, DEBT-044, merged Oct 28 10:24 UTC). The earlier base `f13bfde` is superseded.\n- **Head (exact):** `f60b402fe4b58457d3e23dfdb446744837d218c1` = the original head `4059467` plus ONE merge commit of `main` `6e41187`: no conflicts, no hand edits. The PR's diff against `main` is unchanged (same 15 files, 2679 insertions / 356 deletions). `main` is an ancestor of the head, so the PR is a fast-forward of `main`.\n- **Source:** `remediate/ctx-auth-002-from-f13bfde-local-oct2026` (`7b57cf1`) plus ONE commit, `4059467`, that changes wording only (below). Nothing else was added.\n- **Scope:** 15 files vs `main`. ADR-KERNEL-08 + index row; `core/cognitive/intent.py`, `core/cognitive/planner.py` and their tests; `live_citation_check.py`, `tests/test_live_citation_check.py`, `scripts/mutation_check_ctx_auth_002.py`; threat-model and runbook docs; register / `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` / `CURRENT_STATE.md` entries.\n\n### The one reconciliation commit (`4059467`, docs only)\nTwo sync entries said the line was \"local, not published; no PR\", still needed \"a separate authorization to open a PR\", and pointed at a \"closure report\" that is not in the repository. Those become false or unreachable once this PR exists. Reworded neutrally in `CURRENT_STATE.md` and the DEBT-019 row of `KNOWN_ISSUES.md`. **No status, decision or evidence claim changed.**\n\n## Status (unchanged by this PR)\n\n| Item | Status |\n|---|---|\n| CTX-AUTH-001b | **OPEN** |\n| CTX-AUTH-002 | **not closed** |\n| ADR-KERNEL-08 | **APPROVED (Oct 6, by Moncif), not IMPLEMENTED**. The ADR text still says \"not promoted to `main`\"; moving it to IMPLEMENTED is a separate follow-up after merge and re-verification **on `main`** (ADR §8.1 item 4). I did not edit the approved ADR text. |\n\n## Exact-head verification (clean worktree at `f60b402`, Python 3.12.3, `chromadb==0.5.3`), re-run Oct 28 after reconciliation\n\nThe earlier results on `4059467` (2156 passed, same gates) are superseded by these.\n\n| Check | Command | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Full suite | `python3 -m pytest tests -q -p no:cacheprovider --timeout=90 -rfE` | **2168 passed, 1 xfailed, 0 failed** |\n| Baseline `main` `6e41187`, same command | same | 2084 passed, 1 xfailed, 0 failed (+84 = this PR's tests) |\n| Drift | `python3 scripts/check_drift.py` | no FAIL |\n| Mutation | `python3 scripts/mutation_check_ctx_auth_002.py` | **43/43 caught**; files byte-identical after the run |\n| Harness, six stand-in models | `python3 live_citation_check.py --dry-run {compliant,omit,obey-honest,obey-fabricate,obey-bait,obey-padded} --requests 10 --trials 3` | all exit 0 |\n| Combined with PR #94's head `4f3dc6e` (throwaway merge) | full suite + drift | clean merge; **2247 passed** (= 2084 + 84 + 79), 1 xfailed; drift no FAIL |\n| Tree state after gates | `git status --short` | clean |\n\nThe one `xfailed` is pre-existing and also on `main`.\n\n## What this does NOT establish\n\n- **ADR §8.1 item 1 is still OPEN:** the owner's independent review of `live_citation_check.py`, including exit codes and escalation accounting. The harness is the owner's file and was rewritten.\n- **ADR §8.1 item 2 is still OPEN:** a real-model run on a machine with a configured provider (R3, R5). Every harness run above uses `--dry-run` scripted stand-ins: they validate the harness and the code path, **not any model**, and are labelled \"NOT real-provider evidence\" by the harness itself.\n- The default coverage policy (one exposed, answered trial per payload) is unchanged; changing it is the owner's decision.\n- This environment has `chromadb`, so the `chromadb`-dependent failures other status entries record do not occur here; that does not describe CI's environment. CI results on this head are the authority for CI.\n\n**Please do not merge until §8.1 items 1 and 2 are dispositioned by the owner.** Opening the PR is the owner's instruction; merge readiness is not claimed.\n",
