    "body": "**Identifier change (Oct 27, 2026).** This PR first recorded its work under `DEBT-029`. On `main`, `DEBT-029` is a different finding (the `PlannerWorker._run()` retry-duplication defect, Sept 16, Packet D D-5), and this PR had rewritten that row in place. Commit `de9b222` restores main's `DEBT-029` row verbatim (plus one cross-reference sentence), registers this work as **DEBT-044** (next free identifier on `main`, open PRs, all remote refs and issues at the time) and renames the test file to `tests/test_debt_044_context_persistence.py`. No code change, no status change.\n\n**Open decision for the owner (not made here):** this PR's Step 8 guard changes the same call site main's `DEBT-029` names. Whether that satisfies DEBT-029's own narrow fix is a separate disposition; DEBT-029 is untouched.\n\n**Exact-head verification (`de9b222`, clean tree):** full suite `python3 -m pytest tests -q -p no:cacheprovider --timeout=90` = 2084 passed, 1 xfailed, 0 failed (baseline `main` f13bfde: 2072 passed, 1 xfailed; +12 = this PR's tests); `scripts/check_drift.py` no FAIL. Commit messages of earlier commits on this branch still say `debt-029`; history was not rewritten.\n\n---\nRemediate DEBT-044: ContextMemory.save() SQLite transaction safety, best-effort history persistence containment across K4.2 and legacy orchestrator/planner paths, deterministic regression tests, and debt register retry-reachability reconciliation.\n\n---\n*PR created automatically by Jules for task [4372039021546723617](https://jules.google.com/task/4372039021546723617) started by @1h0lde4*",
