  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/85",
    "id": 4903545778,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABJEYrsg",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/85",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/85.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/85.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/85",
    "number": 85,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "docs: withdraw the unsupported claim that containment options A and B stay inside D-5",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "## Docs: withdraw the unsupported claim that containment options A and B \"stay inside\" D-5\n\n**Status:** ready for review; **not merged**. Documentation only: two files, no code, test, configuration or contract change. Independent of PR #82 (different files) and of the Verification 3C-B branch. Merging requires Moncif's explicit authorization through `premerge_guard.py` pinned to the head SHA.\n\n### What was wrong\nThe ADR (§10.4, containment-options bullet) and the live-check result record (Disposition options) said that, because D-5 says an ESCALATE *\"may\"* surface a question paired with the plan/intent, **options A and B stay inside D-5**. That inference was mine and is not supported by the text:\n- *\"may\"* makes surfacing the question conditional; it does not make the plan pairing optional.\n- ADR §10.3 (Moncif, 2026-09-29) records the question as *\"paired with the concrete interpreted plan/intent required by K4.2\"* and states *\"K4.2 is **not** superseded\"*. K4.2's clarification-policy paragraph describes the existing escalation-surfacing as showing *\"a concrete plan with its stated interpretation, not an abstract disambiguation question\"* (descriptive, applied by D-5); the builder's docstring in `content_anchor.py` says *\"not an abstract question alone\"*.\n- Options A and B remove the plan; C and D retain it. So the existing wording does **not establish** that A and B conform.\n\n### What this PR does\n- Replaces the assertion, **in both records**, with a dated correction (2026-10-17) that records the textual evidence and leaves one question explicitly **unresolved and owned by Moncif**: does the plan-pairing requirement apply to this response path? If binding, A and B need to be excluded or the wording explicitly revised; if not, D-5/K4.2 must be reconciled to make that boundary clear.\n- Says in the result record that it concerns plan pairing only and does not resolve the separate defect that the stated interpretation is the raw request (33 of 33 escalating rows).\n\n### What it deliberately does not do\nNo option is accepted, excluded or selected; the ADR stays **PROPOSED**; all options stay as written (the ADR still lists A–C and the result record still defines D); the author's earlier reading that favored B is left as recorded (it was recorded before the repeated runs and \"neither selects nor excludes any option\"); nothing from the verification (D2/D6/D7, Q4) work is brought into `main`.\n\n### Verification\nThe same claim does not appear anywhere else on `main` (searched `docs`, `CURRENT_STATE.md`, `KNOWN_ISSUES.md`, `core`). `check_drift.py` passes; the runbook-validator tests pass; the two corrected paragraphs were read in place.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-10-17T20:11:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-18T13:47:59Z",
