    "body": "## B02 — re-earn `NET_NAMESPACE` (TC-16, gate G2)\n\nBatch B02 of the `sandbox-network-isolation` workstream (spec §16 B02, §14 TC-16, INV-5). Based on `sandbox-network-isolation/b01-base` (`c357070`, the merge of PR #78).\n\n### What changes\n- `tests/core/sandbox/test_docker_backend.py`: new TC-16 section (3 tests) and two capability tests updated where the contract changed (set 7 → 8, count 7 → 8; `NET_NAMESPACE` moved out of the \"deliberately absent\" list and asserted present).\n- `core/sandbox/backends/docker_backend.py`: `SandboxCapability.NET_NAMESPACE` added to `_CAPS` in the same change (**8 of 12**), plus docstring/comment text. No logic change.\n- `docs/architecture/sandbox-execution-fabric-existing-code-reconciliation.md`: new §21 (OD-6 evidence record); §17.3, §17.8, §18.2 (B2 row), §18.3, §18.5, §18.6, §18.7, §18.8 amended, and a §19 addendum marking the §19.4 statements superseded as to `NET_NAMESPACE` only.\n\n### What TC-16 proves\nFour sandboxes are created concurrently (two without network, two with `allowed_hosts`) and kept running. Each sandbox's network-namespace identity (`net:[inode]`) is read by two observers (inside the sandbox, and `/proc/<init pid>/ns/net` on the host) and must (a) differ from every host reading and from a `--network host` container, and (b) differ pairwise from the others. A `--network host` control proves the probe can see sameness. A pure-logic test pins the separation rule: with `NET_NAMESPACE` claimed, the real `check_admission()` still rejects an `allowed_hosts` request, now on the `NETWORK_ALLOWLIST` check.\n\n### ⚠️ `NET_NAMESPACE` is NOT isolation evidence\nIt means one thing: each sandbox has a network namespace of its own. It does **not** mean a sandbox cannot reach the host or another sandbox. Sandboxes with `allowed_hosts` still share one bridge network and the host gateway (DEBT-039, DEBT-040), and the B01 contract suite is still red for exactly that. Do not cite this claim for `NETWORK_ALLOWLIST`, C2 or any security gate. The same warning is in the `_CAPS` comment and the module docstring.\n\n### Follow-up commit `6f02655` (2026-10-17): the claim and its evidence are unchanged\n- **No implicit image pull.** The `--network host` control used a plain `docker run`, which pulls a missing image (demonstrated: the daemon sent `HEAD https://registry-1.docker.io/…`). It now asserts the image is present locally and runs with `--pull never`; with a missing image it fails with an explicit harness message and 0 pull-related daemon log lines.\n- **Stale statements fixed** (comments and documents only): the `docker_backend.py` module docstring no longer says C2's isolation is \"real and tested\" (C2 is FAIL); two A1 test comments described the pre-B02 state; reconciliation §18 B2 row and sibling statements now reflect 8 claims and TC-16.\n\n### What does not change\n- `NETWORK_ALLOWLIST` stays withdrawn; C2 stays FAIL; A1 stays BLOCKED (A1's three paired-claim tests are unchanged and pass).\n- DEBT-039 and DEBT-040 stay open; no debt closed or registered; `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` / `CURRENT_STATE.md` untouched.\n- B01 suite untouched (`5 passed, 8 xfailed`); `admission.py` untouched; no topology change; no known-failure entry, retry, sleep or weakened assertion.\n- Closure tally (22 PASS / 1 FAIL / 3 BLOCKED / 1 UNVERIFIED / 1 EXCEPTION ACCEPTED) unchanged.\n\n### Evidence (details and limits in reconciliation §21)\nHost: kernel `6.18.44-fc-v139`, Docker 29.8.2, `iptables v1.8.10 (nf_tables)`, Python 3.13.16, image `ocbrain-test/base:local`. Not provisioned (irrelevant: TC-16 uses host gate D only).\n\n| Check (clean committed tree `6f02655`; the head adds one document-only commit) | Result |\n|---|---|\n| TC-16, `-k tc16` | 3 passed; 8 further repeats: 3 passed each |\n| Claim withheld (first pass; test present, `_CAPS` at 7) | 2 passed, 1 failed (`NET_NAMESPACE in supported`) — red before the claim |\n| Mutation: every sandbox `--network host` (repeated) | FAILED: sandbox is in the host's namespace |\n| Mutation: all sandboxes join one shared namespace (repeated) | FAILED: concurrent sandboxes share a namespace |\n| Missing image (`…/b02-missing:none`) | harness failure, 0 pull-related daemon log lines (plain `docker run` contacts the registry) |\n| Full `tests/core/sandbox` | 161 passed, 8 xfailed, twice (baseline 158 + 3 new; same 8 B01 xfails) |\n| `test_network_isolation_contract.py` alone | 5 passed, 8 xfailed |\n| Without Docker on `PATH` | 1 passed, 2 skipped (`requires a reachable Docker daemon`) |\n| `python3 scripts/check_drift.py` | 15/15 PASS (also on the head) |\n| mypy on the 2 changed Python files | no issues (5 pre-existing errors elsewhere, untouched) |\n| Cleanup | 0 containers, 4 networks after every run; one unexplained `iptables-save` digest observation is recorded honestly in §21.3 |\n\nObserved identities: host `net:[4026531833]`; sandboxes `…268`, `…324`, `…380`, `…436`, with both observers agreeing.\n\n### Not run / limits\n- No PR-triggered CI runs for PRs into `b01-base` (workflows run for PRs into `main`); this relies on the recorded local evidence above.\n- Identity is meaningful only between simultaneously live namespaces; four concurrent sandboxes of two shapes were exercised; reachability is out of scope (that is B01's red suite).\n- The backend's own `docker create` carries no `--pull never` (its image is resolved from local `RepoDigests`); an older A9 test runs `docker run` on a fixed local tag. Neither is in B02's scope; noted in §21.5.\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01RzVx1NSzXF1YokR8a8PPiA\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
