    "body": "## Documentation pass: ADR-KERNEL-07 workstream state, DEBT-042/043, runbook status\n\n**Status:** ready for review; **not merged**. Documentation only: no code, config, contract or ADR-status change. Merging requires Moncif's explicit authorization through `premerge_guard.py` pinned to the head SHA.\n\n**Owner of this pass:** the Claude session that did the ADR-KERNEL-07 work (one designated owner, fresh branch from `main`, each file re-read immediately before editing; `main` moved once during the work and was merged in — `488129b`, a one-line result-record wording fix by another session — with no conflict).\n\n### Files (3)\n1. `CURRENT_STATE.md` — a new \"Last synchronized\" entry and one row in the Cognitive Front-End status table. ADR-KERNEL-07 is **PROPOSED, not accepted**; slice 1 is merged behind `creative_content_anchor_enabled` (default `false`, `config/settings.toml:28`); PRs #41 (`ecddbff`), #61 (`4b90ed9`), #45 (`3f8ef97`); the evidence covers **one model and one tested commit** (`e305f20`): C1 FAIL, C2–C4 PASS, Overall FAIL; the C3 human review covered the flagged steps and the joke plans, not all 252 steps; containment options A–D **UNDECIDED** (A–C are in ADR §10.4; D = keep as is is defined only in the result record's \"Disposition options\"); a rerun on current `main` and the access-controlled archive copy are pending; green CI is not evidence of architectural acceptance.\n2. `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` — **DEBT-042** (`_fts_escape()` leaves most FTS5 syntax characters unescaped) and **DEBT-043** (three defects in the clarification response). Both OPEN, neither fixed here.\n3. `docs/studies/OCBRAIN_LIVE_CHECK_DRAFT_PLAN_RUNBOOK_OCT2026.md` — its opening paragraph said \"UNKNOWN … never been run against a real model\" and \"can be read from this branch/PR\"; both were stale. It now says OBSERVED for one model, not settled, and points to the result record, the repeat tool and its protocol (all on `main`). Method steps unchanged.\n\n### What was re-verified for the new entries (2026-10-14, on `main`)\n- **DEBT-042:** reproduced against real SQLite 3.45.1 FTS5 with an explicit set of 14 realistic queries (listed in the entry): **9 of 14** raise `fts5: syntax error`; double-quoting every token (embedded `\"` doubled) fails 0 of 14 — a check, not an applied fix. The earlier session's query set was not preserved; the equal figure was not relied on. The failure is caught and only logged at `core/memory/unified_memory.py:715-716`, so the FTS5 leg contributes no candidates while the L2 vector leg still runs.\n- **DEBT-043:** run against the real builder for several artifact kinds. (a) the \"interpretation\" is `intent.raw_request` (`core/cognitive/intent.py:1090`, passed at `core/orchestrator.py:507-511`) and equals the request in 33 of 33 escalating rows of the committed evidence archive; (b) `\"; \".join(f\"{i}. {t}\")` (`content_anchor.py:321`) produces `….; 2. …`; (c) the example text at `content_anchor.py:296` is identical for every artifact kind.\n- **IDs:** DEBT-042/043 are free on `main`, in open PRs and in remote branch names.\n\n### Deliberately not touched\n`IMPLEMENTATION_ROADMAP.md` (no entry for this workstream; last edited 2026-09-16), the ADR and its status, product code (the `_fts_escape` fix and the response-text fixes need their own PRs from `main`), and the outdated handoff branch (never to be merged).\n\n### One correction to an earlier statement\nAn earlier version of the #45 result record said `compare.json` was byte-identical when recomputed with the final tool. That was wrong: only `report.md` is; `compare.json` gains the one field `evaluation.model_identity`. Another session corrected the record in PR #80; I re-ran the comparison independently and confirm the corrected wording (no shared value differs; one added field).\n\n### Review follow-up (2026-10-17): where option D is defined\nA review found that the new entries said \"containment options A–D\" while ADR-KERNEL-07 §10.4 lists only (A), (B), (C). Verified on `main`: option **D (\"keep as is\")** is defined, together with A–C, in the result record's **\"Disposition options\"** table; the ADR does not list D, and the repeat-run protocol only says that it decides nothing about options A–D. Nothing was invented and no option or ADR status changed: every use of \"A–D\" in this PR now names its source (commit `30236d7`), and DEBT-043 no longer attributes A–D to ADR §10.4. Whether the ADR should also list D is a separate, optional alignment (not done here; it would be a one-line ADR edit for the owner to decide).\n\n**Date correction:** an earlier version of this description dated the follow-up 2026-10-16; the correction was made and pushed on 2026-10-17 (commit `30236d7`). The sync entries in `CURRENT_STATE.md` and `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` keep Oct 14 as the original snapshot and now carry a dated Oct 17 follow-up (commit `57f4eea`), which also states that the containment options A–D are distinct from the resolved D-5 architectural placement \"Option C\" (ADR §10.3, 2026-09-29).\n\n### Open question handled separately: PR #85 (merged)\nA later review pointed out that the result record and ADR §10.4 said containment options A and B \"stay inside\" D-5, whereas D-5's recorded text says an ESCALATE question is *\"paired with the concrete interpreted plan/intent required by K4.2\"* and that *\"K4.2 is not superseded\"*. That unsupported claim was withdrawn in **PR #85, merged on 2026-10-18 as `ef426e9d8fb14dae10c19c2344ceb24d0f04eb81`** (documentation only; no option accepted, excluded or selected). Whether the plan-pairing requirement applies to this response path remains an **owner decision**; the interpretation defect (DEBT-043 (a)) is a separate matter. This PR does not touch either.\n\n### Branch update after #85\n`main` (`ef426e9`) was merged into this branch with a normal merge; the previously reviewed head `57f4eea` is an ancestor of the new tip, and the footprint against `main` is still exactly the three files above.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-10-16T08:32:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-19T08:59:14Z",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-19T08:59:14Z",
    "merged_at": "2026-10-19T08:59:14Z",
