    "body": "## What\n\nOne row of `docs/studies/OCBRAIN_LIVE_CHECK_DRAFT_PLAN_RESULT_OCT2026.md` (the \"Recomputation\" row of the validity table) said that `report.md` and `compare.json` are byte-identical to the supplied archive with both the `e305f20` tool and the final `7044fdb` tool. That is accurate for `report.md` only.\n\n## Evidence (recomputed on the committed archive, offline)\n\n| Tool | `report.md` | `compare.json` |\n|---|---|---|\n| `e305f20` | byte-identical | byte-identical |\n| final (`7044fdb`, identical to `main`) | byte-identical | differs by one added field, `evaluation.model_identity` = `{status: unchanged, established: true, before/after: 365c0bd3c000}`; the verdict (FAIL on C1) and every other field are unchanged |\n\nThe extra field is the Deviation 2 identity record, so this is the expected effect of that rule. Line 145 of the same document already states only `report.md` for the final tool.\n\nReproduce: extract `docs/studies/evidence/live-check-draft-plan-batch-20261012T121543Z.zip`, run `python scripts/live_check_repeat.py compare live_runs/20261012T121543Z` with each tool version, and `cmp` the two output files against the archived ones.\n\n## Scope\n\nOne row, +1/-1, documentation only. No change to code, config, tests, the evidence archive, the ADR (still PROPOSED) or the verdicts.\n\n## Merge\n\nNot merged by the author of this PR. Merging requires the repository owner's explicit authorization and the pre-merge procedure, tied to this exact head.\n",
