    "body": "## B01: network-isolation contract suite, written red\n\nBatch B01 of the `sandbox-network-isolation` workstream (spec ruling OD-7; `docs/architecture/sandbox-network-isolation-master-specification.md` §16 B01). It writes the mechanism-independent definition of \"isolated\" (INV-1: a networked sandbox can reach, from its network, only its own proxy endpoint) as executable tests **before any mechanism exists**.\n\n**Status: IMPLEMENTED and VERIFIED in the scope below. No gate is earned and nothing is closed.** DEBT-039 and DEBT-040 stay open, C2 stays FAIL, the closure tally (22 PASS / 1 FAIL / 3 BLOCKED / 1 UNVERIFIED / 1 EXCEPTION ACCEPTED) and `_CAPS` (7 of 12) are unchanged.\n\n### Change set (2 commits)\n- `694ba2a` adds `tests/core/sandbox/test_network_isolation_contract.py` (new file, nothing else in code).\n- `d3af4ef` adds §20 to the reconciliation document: the OD-6 evidence record. Documentation only.\n\nOut of scope and untouched: `contracts.py`, `admission.py`, `_net_proxy.py`, `docker_backend.py`, `namespace_backend.py`, the frozen addendum and checklist, any new `SandboxCapability`.\n\n### What the suite does\n| Case | Variants | Red today because |\n|---|---|---|\n| TC-01 / TC-02 | TCP, UDP | a host service bound to `0.0.0.0` is reachable through the gateway (DEBT-040, F6) |\n| TC-03 | handed port, scan, CONNECT, plain HTTP | B uses A's proxy (DEBT-039, F1 to F4) |\n| TC-04 | sibling proxy, host primary address | a test-owned `NET_RAW` container on B's network gets a SYN-ACK from a crafted frame (F28: DEBT-039, DEBT-040), with a positive control to B's own endpoint |\n\nEach case calls `create()` directly, asserts that its setup fired and its controls held, reads to EOF (reusing `_recv_to_eof`, never a single `recv()`), uses only host-local loopback upstreams (hermetic), and checks Docker containers, networks and the firewall against the start-of-test baseline.\n\n**Red for the right reason.** Every variant carries `xfail(strict=True, raises=<DebtNNNViolation>)`; the violation classes are raised only by the contract assertion, so harness errors, failed controls and ordinary assertions fail loudly. `strict=True` forces the batch that earns a gate to remove the marker in the same change (never the known-failures manifest). Meta-tests (no Docker) check every variant.\n\n### Evidence (OD-6 record is §20 of the reconciliation document)\n- Final commit of the test: `694ba2a14e408c1c9930f0d863caa0cd14d231bf`; base `d5de7baf0ff32d0d6c68f4b597d0d442a5e023b6`.\n- Host: kernel `6.18.44-fc-v114`, Docker 29.8.2, `iptables v1.8.10 (nf_tables)`, Python 3.13.16, pytest 9.1.1; not provisioned.\n- Command: `OCBRAIN_SANDBOX_DOCKER_IMAGE=ocbrain-test/base:local env -u NO_PROXY -u no_proxy python3 -m pytest tests/core/sandbox/test_network_isolation_contract.py -v -rxXs -p no:cacheprovider`\n- Result on the clean committed tree, 2026-10-13T11:05:14Z: `5 passed, 8 xfailed in 25.94s`; containers, networks and firewall identical before and after.\n- With the markers withdrawn (host declared provisioned, no mechanism): `8 failed` and each failure is the intended violation class (messages in §20.3).\n- Six harness-fault mutations (broken probe, loose marker, wrong exception class, equal allowlists, silent probe, attacker without `NET_RAW`) all FAIL loudly, never XFAIL.\n- A throwaway scratch firewall (verbatim in §20.6, not committed, not a mechanism proposal) made all 13 cases pass, and made the 8 marked variants XPASS(strict) without the declaration; no scratch rule remained afterward.\n- Skip with reason: no `docker` binary, or image absent: `8 skipped, 5 passed`.\n- Full sandbox suite, 3 runs: `158 passed, 8 xfailed` each (the 153 of the `d5de7ba` revalidation + 5 meta-tests + the 8 expected-red variants). `mypy` (new file; `core/sandbox`) clean; `python3 scripts/check_drift.py` 15 of 15 PASS; 0 orphan containers or networks.\n- Limits: one host in one adjusted environment (as recorded for `d5de7ba`); the red state is demonstrated unprovisioned, never on a provisioned host; nothing is claimed about `NamespaceBackend` (TC-17 is B04).\n\n### Impact review (PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS §18.3)\n- Architecture, governance, replay, observability: none; tests only. Security: no control added or weakened; the suite measures one. Compatibility and migration: none. Rollback: revert the two commits.\n- The suite starts containers on the host Docker daemon and a `NET_RAW` attacker container (removed in `finally`); it needs no privileges beyond the Docker socket and reads `iptables-save` when available.\n\n### Interpretations for you to confirm (not rulings; details in §20.6)\n1. **P gate**: `OCBRAIN_SANDBOX_NETWORK_PROVISIONED=1` is my interim declaration until B10's verify mode exists. It can only make the suite stricter.\n2. TC-03 \"scan\" = TCP connect scan of the gateway over `{3128} ∪` the ephemeral range, with a control that it finds B's own endpoint (not a scan of the Docker address pool).\n3. TC-04 is split into two variants (one per debt, each with its own typed marker); its positive control is network-scoped (rule S2), so a source-address-keyed mechanism would fail that control loudly.\n4. **Base branch**: opened against `sandbox-network-isolation/b01-base` (= `sandbox-fabric` = `d5de7ba`). If you prefer `sandbox-fabric` as the target, say so and I will retarget.\n\n**Not merged.** This PR is merged only on an explicit instruction.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01RzVx1NSzXF1YokR8a8PPiA\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01RzVx1NSzXF1YokR8a8PPiA)_",
