  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/75",
    "id": 4819640196,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABH0XfhA",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/75",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/75.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/75.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/75",
    "number": 75,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "test(sandbox): make the C2 allowed-host tunnel test hermetic (host-local upstream)",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "Test-only change. Makes `test_c2_allowed_host_reaches_the_real_server_through_the_tunnel` hermetic, as ruled on October 8 2026 (order: docs-only PR #72 -> this PR -> B01). Only `tests/core/sandbox/test_docker_backend.py` changes (+127 −16); no production code, no known-failures entry, no weakened assertion, no retry, no sleep.\n\n## Problem\nThe test fetched `https://example.com/` through the sandbox's `AllowlistProxy`, so its verdict depended on the test host's DNS and egress layer (study F10). On a host where `example.com` does not resolve it fails with `502 Bad Gateway` although the proxy and tunnel are correct. Reproduced red **3 of 3** on `2b568cc` in a fresh VM (`TUNNEL_FAILED Tunnel connection failed: 502 Bad Gateway`).\n\n## Change\n- A real `http.server` on the host's loopback (`_RecordingUpstream`) records every request target and answers `upstream-saw:<target>`. `allowed_hosts=(\"127.0.0.1\",)`; the proxy runs on the host, so it dials that address. (`test_net_proxy.py` already uses the same pattern.)\n- From inside the sandbox the probe opens a **CONNECT tunnel through the proxy named by the sandbox's own `HTTPS_PROXY`**, sends one GET through it and reads the answer to EOF.\n- Assertions: the sandbox received the upstream's own answer, **and** the upstream recorded exactly that one request (a proxy that fabricates a 200 fails), **and** no name resolution was attempted.\n- `no_name_resolution` fixture: any attempt in the test process (the proxy runs there) to resolve a non-numeric name fails like a dead resolver and is reported, so hermeticity is enforced, not assumed.\n- The C2 section comment is updated. The remaining `example.com` / `example.org` mentions in the file are names only: an allowlist entry that is never dialed, or a request the proxy rejects with `403` before dialing. `test_net_proxy.py` was reviewed: its two `example.com` uses are rejected-before-dial tests and everything else dials loopback.\n\n## Evidence (environment: fresh VM, Docker 29.8.2, Python 3.13.16, 1 core; DNS for `example.com` broken, as in the earlier fresh boot)\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Old test on `2b568cc`, 3 runs | **red 3/3**, 502 |\n| New test, 20 consecutive targeted runs | **20/20 pass** (~1.8 s each) |\n| Mutant P1: allowlist rejects everything | allowed-host test **fails**; caught |\n| Mutant P2: fabricated tunnel (200, no real upstream) | **fails**; caught |\n| Mutant P3: upstream-to-client bytes dropped | **fails**; caught |\n| Mutant P4: canned 200 instead of relaying | **fails**; caught |\n| Mutant P5: allowlist open | allowed-host test passes (expected: it is not that test's job); **`test_c2_disallowed_host_is_rejected_at_the_tunnel` fails** |\n| Mutant T1: test names `localhost` | **fails** with the guard live; **passes** with the guard neutralized, so the guard is what enforces hermeticity |\n| Every mutant restored | `git diff` / `cmp` clean after each; `core/` untouched |\n| Full `tests/core/sandbox`, 4 runs | **153 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped**, each run; 0 orphan containers, 0 shared-network endpoints, 0 artifact dirs after each |\n| `mypy` on `docker_backend.py` and `test_docker_backend.py` | no issues |\n| `scripts/check_drift.py` | 15/15 PASS |\n\nCommands: `python3 -m pytest tests/core/sandbox -q --asyncio-mode=auto -p no:cacheprovider -rfs --tb=short` with `OCBRAIN_SANDBOX_DOCKER_IMAGE=ocbrain-test/base:local`.\n\n## Environment findings (not caused by this change; classified per PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS §16.4)\nOn the **untouched** `2b568cc` in this VM, `NamespaceBackend` tests also failed, for reasons that are properties of the VM and were each confirmed causally:\n1. `/usr/bin/python3` is a symlink into `/etc/alternatives`, which the namespace jail does not bind (it binds only `/bin /lib /lib64 /usr`), so `execvp` of `python3` / `sys.executable` fails inside the jail: 8 failures in `test_namespace_backend.py` and 2 in `test_allowed_hosts.py`. With the interpreter reached by its real path, all pass.\n2. The VM exports `NO_PROXY`/`no_proxy` containing `127.0.0.1`, inherited into the namespace sandbox, so urllib bypasses the proxy for the loopback target: 1 failure (`test_allowed_host_is_reachable_through_the_proxy`). With them unset, it passes.\n3. `iproute2` and `gcc-multilib` were absent (4 + 1 tests skipped); installed.\nThe 153-pass runs above used `/usr/bin/python3` as a direct symlink to `python3.13`, `NO_PROXY`/`no_proxy` unset, and those two packages installed. Note for later: finding 1 is also a real, by-design limitation of the jail (an interpreter reached through a symlink outside the four bound trees cannot be exec'd); it is recorded, not registered as a debt.\n\n## Limits (stated plainly)\n- One environment, one load profile (no run under CPU load). The verdict is about this one test's dependence on external DNS, not about the whole suite under every host.\n- The test image here was rebuilt from this VM's rootfs without heavy unrelated trees (`ocbrain-test/base:local`, Python 3.13), not the earlier image.\n- This does **not** change C2's status (FAIL, DEBT-039) or any other checklist item; `sandbox-fabric` stays explicitly incomplete.\n\nMerge as a **merge commit**, guarded by the head SHA.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01RzVx1NSzXF1YokR8a8PPiA\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01RzVx1NSzXF1YokR8a8PPiA)_",
