    },
    "body": "Documentation only; no code or contract change. Records the owner decisions of 2026-10-10 and the state after PR #73.\n\n## Changes (additive)\n- `KNOWN_ISSUES.md`, `CURRENT_STATE.md`: new Oct 10 \"Last synchronized\" entries.\n  - **#65:** PR #73 (merge commit `77e2e82`) pinned `chromadb==0.5.3` in `pyproject.toml` and added a pin-agreement test. The pin is provisional pending the planned compatibility study.\n  - **#70 (Dependabot #4):** boundary decision now (option 1) with its reopen triggers; upgrade (option 3) recorded as the direction, unscheduled. Includes the note that the advisory's fix version is 5.6.0 but the gate behavior changes in 6.0.0. States what the assessment did not verify.\n  - Dependabot #1-#4 all remain open; nothing dismissed; PRs #32/#33 untouched.\n- `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` DEBT-032 row: Oct 10 addendum appended (existing text byte-identical as a prefix; still 5 table cells).\n\n## One correction to an earlier statement\nThe Oct 6 entry's \"K4.2 empty-answer gap on workflow failure\" is the already-registered **FZ-01** (`wf_result.output or \"\"`, no failure channel; blocked on maintainer decision D1, depends on FZ-02). My earlier handoff said no work item existed; that was wrong because the register already tracks it. **No duplicate item was created** and FZ-01's status is unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n- Post-merge `main` @ `77e2e82`: `tests`, `drift-and-ownership`, both `Analyze` jobs success; code scanning 0 open / 34 fixed / 4 dismissed (same 4 from Oct 2, none by this work).\n- `scripts/check_drift.py`: exit 0. Both files LF; diff is +3/-1 (the -1 is the DEBT-032 row rewritten with the addendum appended).\n- Test figures quoted are local sandbox runs, not CI's.\n\nNot merging without an explicit go-ahead for the exact head.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-10-10T10:52:08Z",
