    },
    "body": "Closes the declaration half of #65. Owner decision: https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/65#issuecomment-6096538690 (pin exactly for now; revisit after the planned compatibility study).\n\n## Change\n- `pyproject.toml`: `chromadb>=0.4.0,<1.0` -> `chromadb==0.5.3` (now matches `requirements.txt:4` and the three `pip install` lines in `release.yml`).\n- `tests/test_chromadb_pin_agreement.py` (new, 4 tests): `requirements.txt`, `pyproject.toml` and every `pip install ... chromadb` line in `release.yml` must be exact `==` pins that agree with each other. The version is **not** hard-coded, so the study can change all three together.\n\n## Evidence (local sandbox, Python 3.12.3, not CI)\n- New tests: 4 passed. Against `main`'s `pyproject.toml`: 2 failed, 2 passed.\n- Mutation check: 10 mutants (drifted/unpinned/range/removed in each of the three files, one release line drifting, one unpinned, all release lines losing chromadb), all caught (10 of 10).\n- `scripts/check_drift.py`: exit 0. Only `pyproject.toml` metadata and a new test file changed; no runtime code.\n- CI is the authority for the full suite; I did not re-run it here.\n\n## Scope and limits\n- Does **not** dismiss Dependabot #1-#3 (`chromadb`); they stay open per the owner's decision.\n- Does not touch `sentence-transformers` (#70) or Dependabot PRs #32/#33.\n- The Android p4a `--requirements` list in `release.yml` names `chromadb` without a version; it is not a pip pin and is not covered (documented in the test docstring).\n- The pin is provisional.\n\nNot merging without an explicit go-ahead for the exact head.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-10-10T10:25:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-10T10:45:43Z",
