  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/71",
    "id": 4783677496,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABHSEgOA",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/71",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/71.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/71.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/71",
    "number": 71,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "fix(FZ-02/B2b): stalled and hard-deadline generations fail and keep their partial text",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "**FZ-02, batch B2b only.** Implements decision **D2=(i)**: a stalled or hard-deadline generation is a failure that carries its partial text. B2a (provider failures) is already on `main`.\n\n**Invariant:** only STALLED and HARD_DEADLINE change; every other existing outcome keeps its current semantics.\n\n## Defect\n`ModelRouterAdapter.execute()` returned `success=True` for `STALLED` and `HARD_DEADLINE` outcomes (pinned unchanged in B2a). A stalled stream reported its half-finished text as a successful answer; a stream that never produced a token reported an empty success.\n\n## Change (`core/capabilities/adapters/model_router_adapter.py`)\n- `STALLED` and `HARD_DEADLINE` leave the pinned set: `success=False`, `output=None`, a fixed opaque error, failure metadata (`failure_type`, `retryable`) and the partial text in `metadata[\"partial_output\"]` when there is any. Partial text is never placed in `output` (same convention as the B2a provider-failure result).\n- Still pinned unchanged: `COMPLETED_WITH_PARTIAL_OUTPUT` (defined, but `route()` never produces it, and D2=(i) does not cover it) and `EMPTY_RESPONSE` (PR #67 ruling).\n- `route()` is untouched: its classification and the answer text consumers see are exactly as before (pinned by a test).\n- `_UNCHANGED_BY_B2A` renamed `_PINNED_UNCHANGED`.\n\n## Tests\n- New `tests/test_fz02_stalled_deadline_failure.py` (8 tests): adapter matrix of {stalled, hard_deadline} x {partial, none}; three end-to-end scenarios through the real router (hung stream, endless stream under a tiny hard ceiling, no first token); a `route()`-unchanged pin.\n- B2a's pin test no longer pins STALLED/HARD_DEADLINE (parametrization 4 -> 2): an intended change, since B2b changes exactly those.\n\n## Evidence\n- Red/green: 7 of the new tests fail on the unchanged adapter with genuine `success=True` results (e.g. a stalled stream returned `output='Beginning the tale'`); all pass after.\n- 26 related test files: 456 passed before, **462 passed** after (456 - 2 removed pins + 8 new), 1 xfailed both.\n- Full suite (run alone): 8 failed / 1968 passed / 4 errors before; **8 failed / 1974 passed / 4 errors** after; identical failing set of 12 pre-existing ids.\n- `scripts/check_drift.py`: 15/15. All touched files LF.\n\n## Interim effect for the reviewer (FZ-01 is not fixed here)\nMeasured end to end (`PlannerWorker` -> `AdapterRuntime` -> real adapter and router, only the stream and budget replaced):\n- **Stall with partial text:** before, the user saw the truncated text `'Once upon a time, a brave knight'` (with no signal it was cut); after, the user sees `[Error in coding: RuntimeError (ref ...)]`, and the partial text lives in adapter metadata only. It reaches the user once the result channel (B3/B4, D1=(a)) carries it. `PlannerWorker` still reports `success=True` (that is FZ-01).\n- **No first token:** before, a silent empty answer; after, a visible error line. Strictly better.\n\n## Reviewer notes\n1. `route()` labels every non-stall cancellation `HARD_DEADLINE` (deadline, startup window, external cancel), so the failure message for it is deliberately neutral (\"stopped before it completed\"). Pre-existing classification, not changed here.\n2. The adapter's `error` can reach users; it is fixed text, never exception text, hosts or partial text (tested).\n3. Other adapters were not inspected.\n\nReview target: `main` = `8c0ea03` (B2a merge). Branch is intentionally not updated while under review. Merge sequence (agreed): sign-off on this head, then update against `main` with a merge commit, fresh CI/CodeQL, then merge.",
    "created_at": "2026-10-08T07:53:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-09T08:36:31Z",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-09T08:36:31Z",
    "merged_at": "2026-10-09T08:36:31Z",
