  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/68",
    "id": 4770042076,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABHFEQ3A",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/68",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/68.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/68.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/68",
    "number": 68,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "fix(docker-backend): D11 - classify a run killed by destroy() by its cause, not by the timing of the exit-code read",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "## What\n\nFixes a **product defect** found while verifying the D7 test fix (PR #64): `run()` + `destroy()` raced, and under load the run returned `COMPLETED` with exit code 137 instead of the required `ERROR` (reconciliation §19.1 reopened; D11 is **not accepted until this is merged and the loaded verification is clean**). Separate from B01 and from PR #64.\n\n## Cause\n\n`destroy()` kills and removes the container `run()` is waiting on; `run()` then reads the exit code and classifies. If the container is already removed there is nothing to read and the result is `ERROR`; if the read lands between the kill and the removal it sees 137 and the result is `COMPLETED`. Nothing recorded that destroy caused the kill, so the outcome depended on timing.\n\n## Fix (`docker_backend.py`: +22 −1)\n\n- `_DockerRunState.destroy_requested`: set by `destroy()` **before its first await** and **only if the handle is RUNNING** (the D6 lesson, as for `cancel_requested`: a failed destroy of a sandbox that never ran must not mislabel a later run).\n- `_classify` consults it with fixed causal precedence: **OOM kill, requested cancel, requested destroy (ERROR), missing exit code (ERROR), normal completion.** Exit 137 alone still decides nothing.\n- No retry, no sleep stabilization, no weakened assertion, no known-failures entry. The original `test_d11_run_plus_destroy_concurrently_no_hang_no_orphan` is unchanged.\n\n## Both sides of the race are proved\n\n- **Run+destroy gives ERROR whichever comes first:** `test_d11_destroy_during_run_is_error_when_run_reads_exit_137_before_the_removal` forces the old failing interleaving with events and asserts it happened (the read returned 137): **red 8/8 on the unfixed code** with `COMPLETED == ERROR`, **green 15/15 after**. `test_d11_destroy_during_run_is_error_when_the_removal_lands_before_run_reads_the_exit_code` forces the other order (nothing to read): ERROR.\n- **Exit 137 is not misclassified merely for being 137:** `test_d11_a_workload_that_exits_137_by_itself_is_completed_not_error` (a workload that SIGKILLs itself is `COMPLETED`, exit 137); `test_d11_destroying_one_sandbox_does_not_change_another_sandboxs_outcome` (B destroyed while A, which ends by its own SIGKILL, keeps running: A `COMPLETED`/137, B `ERROR`); the existing C1 tests (cancel with 137 is `CANCELLED`) still pass.\n- **Precedence and non-stickiness:** `test_d11_cancel_then_destroy_during_run_is_cancelled`; `test_d11_a_destroy_that_fails_before_any_run_does_not_mislabel_a_later_run`.\n\n## Loaded verification (the condition that exposed it)\n\nSame load as the reproduction (6 concurrent workers, 3 CPU burners, 1-core VM) on the original run+destroy test: **0 failures in 36**, against **17 in 48** on the D7 branch and **3 in 36** on the untouched `sandbox-fabric` tip before the fix.\n\n## Mutation testing of the marker and the classification (all caught; source restored byte-identical each time)\n\n| Mutant | Caught by |\n|---|---|\n| M1 classifier ignores the marker | the forced \"read before removal\" test |\n| M2 marker set only after the removal | the forced test and the failed-destroy test |\n| M3 the forbidden shortcut: exit 137 alone means ERROR | four tests, including the existing C1 cancel test and the self-137 test |\n| M4 marker global instead of per handle | the per-handle independence test |\n| M5 precedence swapped (destroy beats cancel) | the cancel-then-destroy test |\n| M6 marker recorded for any handle state | the failed-destroy test |\n\n(My first form of M2 was a syntax error and therefore invalid; it was corrected and re-run.)\n\n## Other evidence\n\n- Full `tests/core/sandbox`: **6 consecutive runs, 153 passed each (147 + 6 new), 0 failures**; 0 containers, 0 network endpoints and 0 temp directories left after every batch.\n- mypy clean on both files; architecture drift check 15/15.\n- **Commit 1** is documentation: reconciliation §19.1 now records the defect as `DEFECT IDENTIFIED` (historical text kept unedited), with the D11 row, the status vocabulary, the §18 tally (21 PASS, 1 FAIL, 1 DEFECT IDENTIFIED, 3 BLOCKED, 1 UNVERIFIED, 1 EXCEPTION ACCEPTED = 28) and a §19.4 addendum updated; Result 2 is unchanged. The closure evidence is added to §19.1 after this and PR #64 merge.\n- Not run: a full-suite run under load (only the D11 test was loaded).\n\n## Merging\n\nMerge commit only. Sequence ruled by the user: this PR, then PR #64 revalidated on the resulting tip with 0-failure full-suite runs, then the §19.1 closure evidence, then the B01 base branch.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-10-07T08:31:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-07T08:31:24Z",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-07T08:31:24Z",
    "merged_at": "2026-10-07T08:31:24Z",
