    "body": "**FZ-02, batch B2a only.** A provider failure no longer completes as success. Decisions D1=(a) and D2=(i) are **not** implemented here.\n\n**Invariant for B2a:** provider failures become failures; every other existing outcome keeps its current semantics.\n\n## Defect (register FZ-02)\n`_ollama_stream()` swallowed provider errors into an in-band token and returned normally, so a `ConnectError` classified as `SUCCESS`; `ModelRouterAdapter.execute()` then hard-coded `success=True` and ignored `route_result.execution_detail`. Reproduced with the real router and adapter, only the HTTP client faked (before: `failure_type=success`, adapter `success=True` with the error token as its output).\n\n## Change\n- `core/model_router.py`: the error token is now a `ProviderStreamError(str)` with byte-identical `[Error: ...]` text plus an `error_id`, so SSE, `stream_route()` and every other consumer see what they saw before. The signal travels on the token (no shared mutable state). `_call_monitored_streaming()` classifies it as `PROVIDER_FAILURE` and keeps it out of output and partial output. With no marker, behaviour is unchanged.\n- `core/capabilities/adapters/model_router_adapter.py`: classifies a real `ExecutionOutcome` by `failure_type` and fails closed. `SUCCESS` passes; `STALLED` / `HARD_DEADLINE` / `COMPLETED_WITH_PARTIAL_OUTPUT` / `EMPTY_RESPONSE` are explicitly left exactly as before (`success=True`, no new metadata); every other non-success outcome returns `success=False`, `output=None`, a fixed opaque error (+ ref) and failure metadata. Partial text goes to metadata, never to `output`. A `RouteResult` without an `ExecutionOutcome` is unchanged.\n- `tests/test_fz02_provider_failure.py`: 17 tests (new).\n- Commit `0a6d342` is a separate whitespace-only CRLF to LF conversion of `core/model_router.py` (`git diff --ignore-cr-at-eol` is empty); review the logic in `728bbfd` and `c2f6070`.\n\n## Not changed (pinned by tests)\nStalled / deadline / partial semantics (B2b); `EMPTY_RESPONSE` semantics (later outcome-policy work); FZ-01 result channel (B3/B4); FZ-05; other adapters.\n\n## Review history\n- Scope correction from review: `EMPTY_RESPONSE` moved into the pinned set (`c2f6070`), with an adapter-level and an end-to-end test proving `success=True` is preserved. These pinning tests also pass on the untouched `8b0fee2` logic.\n\n## Evidence (corrected head `c2f6070`)\n- Original 16 tests: 10 red / 6 green on the untouched logic. Now 17 tests, all green; the 7 pinning tests also pass on `8b0fee2`.\n- 24 pre-existing related test files: 439 passed / 1 xfailed before and after.\n- Full suite (run alone): 8 failed / 1943 passed / 4 errors before; 8 failed / 1960 passed / 4 errors after (+17 = the new tests; identical failing set of 12 pre-existing ids).\n- `scripts/check_drift.py`: 15/15. CI on this head: `tests`, `drift-and-ownership`, CodeQL all green; CodeQL: no new alerts in code changed by this pull request.\n- End-to-end probe (PlannerWorker -> AdapterRuntime -> real adapter and router, HTTP faked): before the user saw `[Error: model request failed (ref A)]`; after `[Error in coding: RuntimeError (ref B)]`. Worker still reports `success=True` (that is FZ-01), one provider call.\n\n## Reviewer notes\n1. Stalled / hard-deadline outcomes with **no** partial text, and `EMPTY_RESPONSE`, still return `success=True` with an empty answer (pinned).\n2. The adapter's `error` string can reach users (the planner raises it); it is fixed text plus an opaque ref, never exception text or hosts.\n3. Non-monitored branches (`execution_detail=None`): `generate_with_fallback` raises after exhausting providers (`provider_mesh.py:226`), so they already fail loudly. Other adapters were not inspected.\n\n## Merge sequence (agreed)\nReview and sign-off on this head first. Only then: update the branch against current `main` (merge commit), fresh CI/CodeQL, merge. **Not updated yet:** `main` has moved to `58d079f` (PR #63, no file overlap, dry-run merge clean); branch is intentionally not updated while under review.",
    "created_at": "2026-10-07T08:18:26Z",
