  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/63",
    "id": 4751637777,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABGzg9EQ",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/63",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/63.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/63.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/63",
    "number": 63,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "fix(orchestrator): do not return a failed workflow's raw error text as the answer (issue #62, DEBT-037 follow-up)",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "Fixes the leak described in #62 (DEBT-037 follow-up): a failed workflow run no longer hands its raw error text to the caller as the answer. **Not merge-ready until CI and a fresh CodeQL analysis of the final commit are reviewed.**\n\n**Owner:** @1h0lde4. **Baseline:** `main` @ `8b0fee2`.\n\n## Problem (reproduced on `main` before the change)\n`Orchestrator.handle()`'s workflow-runtime branch returned `f\"Sorry, I encountered an internal error: {wf_result.error}\"`. For `PlannerWorker` that string is `\"PlannerWorker pipeline error: <str(exception)>\"`, so any failure in its pipeline put paths/hosts/config values into the `/query` answer.\n\n## Contract (DEBT-037 / `core/error_ref.py` answer-text rule, applied here)\n- **C1** answer is exactly `Sorry, I encountered an internal error: WorkflowFailure (ref <uuid>)`; nothing of `wf_result.error` appears.\n- **C2** the real text is logged server-side under that ref.\n- **C3** internal channels unchanged: the `orchestrator.query_failed` event still carries `wf_result.error`; `WorkerResult.error` and tracing untouched.\n- **C4** the sibling branch (unexpected exception in the workflow path) still returns only the class name; now pinned by a test.\n\n## Change (3 files, +216/-5)\n- `core/orchestrator.py`: that one branch; stays CRLF.\n- `core/error_ref.py`: new `log_text_and_ref()` for failures that exist only as text.\n- `tests/test_workflow_failure_disclosure.py`: 8 new tests.\n\nImplementation choices that are mine, not owner-confirmed (listed in #62): fix at the caller boundary rather than in `PlannerWorker` (single choke point for any node's error string; leaves the internal channel DEBT-037 left alone); the `WorkflowFailure` type token (already this branch's event `error_type`); the new helper.\n\n## Evidence (local)\n- 3 of the 8 tests fail against the unfixed orchestrator; the other 5 pass before and after.\n- 7 mutants (raw error returned, text appended, ref missing, text not logged, constant ref, internal event redacted, sibling branch leaking `str(e)`): all caught.\n- Planner/disclosure tests: 62 passed on Python 3.11.15, 3.12.3, 3.13.13, 3.14.4.\n- Full suite: 8 failed, 1951 passed, 4 skipped, 1 xfailed vs baseline 8 failed, 1943 passed on `8b0fee2`; failing set identical (8 `chromadb` import failures in the sandbox; delta = the 8 new tests).\n\n## Not claimed / out of scope\n- **CodeQL:** no analysis of this commit yet; nothing dismissed.\n- The K4.2 front-end branch never reads `wf_result.error` (it can return an empty answer): a separate documented gap, untouched.\n- DEBT-032 and the `/import` work are separate; registry docs get their own PR after a definitive state.\n\nRefs #62\n",
