    "body": "## Tooling: repeated live-check runs with automatic provenance and a pre-registered comparison\n\n**Status:** ready for review; **not merged**. Merging requires Moncif's explicit authorization, through `premerge_guard.py` pinned to the head SHA. Head at the time of this description: `7044fdb23c490ced85b74232757b045ed91fd707` (CI green on that head: `tests`, `drift-and-ownership`, CodeQL, Analyze x2). No formal GitHub review is recorded on this PR; the review decisions below were given in the working session.\n\n**Scope: three files, tooling and docs only** (no product code, no ADR, no change to PR #45; the harness is byte-identical to `main`):\n1. `scripts/live_check_repeat.py` — runs the existing harness N times; records repo commit and dirty files, Python/platform, SHA-256 of tool and harness, `ollama list`/`ollama show` before and after the batch, per-run UTC times and worker pids; `compare` evaluates the pre-registered criteria.\n2. `docs/studies/OCBRAIN_LIVE_CHECK_REPEAT_RUNS_PROTOCOL_OCT2026.md` — the protocol. Criteria **C1–C4 and every threshold were pre-registered before any repeated-run data existed and are unchanged**. Two later **deviations** are documented in the file: Deviation 1 (execution method and replay guard) and Deviation 2 (model-identity validity rule). Both are validity rules, not criteria, and both are stated as post-hoc.\n3. `tests/test_live_check_repeat.py` — 62 tests (fake harness and fake command runner; real worker processes against a stub harness and against the real harness in `--offline` mode; one test pins the protocol text to the tool's constants).\n\n**History of this branch, in order**\n- `e305f20` — one fresh process per preflight and run; replay guard; dirty files listed; clean abort on worker failure (Deviation 1). **This is the commit that produced evidence batch `20261012T121543Z`** (recorded in PR #45).\n- `5d673d7` — merge of `main` (branch housekeeping).\n- `851d4ee` — replay-guard wording: the 2 s floor and the identical-output rule are described as indirect evidence (\"suspicious / freshness not established\", \"indistinguishable from a replay\"), never as a proven replay (review decision of 2026-10-13). Threshold and post-hoc status unchanged.\n- `7044fdb` — model identity is an evidence-validity rule: a batch whose model ID changed, could not be read before or after, or has no after-batch snapshot is **INSUFFICIENT** and no criterion is evaluated (Deviation 2; found by review, not by data). Real-data regression: the valid batch `20261012T121543Z` still yields FAIL (C1) and a byte-identical `report.md`.\n\n`e305f20` remains an ancestor of the head (merge commit, not squash, is intended so that the tested commit stays reachable from `main`).\n\n**Verification at `7044fdb`:** 62 tests pass; `check_drift.py` passes; offline smoke run with real worker processes passes; CI green. Mutation checks were run for each change (original tool 17; Deviation 1 change 17; wording 3; Deviation 2 10) and all are caught — where one initially survived, the test was strengthened. In the authoring sandbox 30 other tests fail for missing dependencies (the same IDs fail on the unmodified base); they are not part of this change.\n\n**Not decided here:** nothing in this PR decides containment options A–D or accepts ADR-KERNEL-07 (it stays PROPOSED). PASS means \"no contradiction found in these runs\", never proof. Sampling remains uncontrolled by design (the product code sends no temperature or seed).\n\n**Known limits (also in the protocol):** model identity is compared at two points only; the replay guard is a coarse screen; llama3 only, default sampling, one machine.\n",
