    "body": "## B10 — register the Kernel v1.0 freeze-remediation status; fix the known-failure-list header\n\n**Documentation only. No code, test, workflow or contract change.** 2 files: `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` (+45/−1 pure insertions), `docs/architecture/D10_KNOWN_ENVIRONMENTAL_FAILURES.txt` (header comment only).\n\n### What changes\n1. **`KNOWN_ISSUES.md` — new section \"Kernel v1.0 Freeze Remediation (Oct 2026)\"** with a status table for FZ-01..FZ-07:\n   - **FZ-04 (B1, PR #51 → `1a09941`), FZ-03 (B8, PR #53 → `80a1bb8`), FZ-07 (B9, PR #55 → `e438387`): FIXED + VERIFIED**, each with its evidence and its explicit residuals (B8: `cleaner.run_all` still blocks the loop, `print()` handlers unchanged, 60 s floor is a behaviour change, test-suite file mutation; the Graphify result recorded as an *accepted evidence exception*, never \"green on `0ff0937`\").\n   - **FZ-01, FZ-02, FZ-05, FZ-06: OPEN and NOT STARTED**, blocked on D1–D3 as before. They are described as measured, re-confirmed **by code inspection on `e438387`** (still valid on `7464a84`: no cited file changed since) (not by re-running repros), and no outcome is assumed. The D1–D3 options are listed neutrally; none is chosen.\n   - **FZ-07 residual R-1** recorded as an open follow-up (the `FAILED` node-ID ` - ` truncation), plus the two observations (list root-cause label still unverified; the runner's 2 warnings not traced).\n   - The section states in its first paragraph that it is **a status register, not a freeze verdict; no FREEZE READY claim is made or implied.**\n2. **`DEBT-031` addendum** — pure insertion (786 chars). The row called the CI gate \"genuinely, correctly enforced\" while it gated on the allowlist alone; FZ-07 showed otherwise and B9 replaced it. The allowlist root-cause mislabel in that row is untouched and still open.\n3. **`D10_KNOWN_ENVIRONMENTAL_FAILURES.txt` header wording** — now describes the gate as it behaves (exit 0/1 only, errors/INTERNALERROR/empty runs/other exit codes cannot be listed, exact-ID matching, and \"do not add an entry containing ` - `\"). **The 34 entries are not touched.**\n4. A \"Last synchronized\" line.\n\n### Non-goals / explicitly not done\n- **Known-failure list not modified or widened, not pruned.** Proven below.\n- **`CURRENT_STATE.md` untouched.** Its Sept 23 freeze-verdict wording (\"down to REM-004 and CTX-EXPORT-001\") predates the Oct 1 audit and is **not reconciled**; the new section says so in plain words instead of papering over it.\n- **`DEBT-033` text untouched** (it says `main` has no branch protection). Live API on Oct 5 shows required checks `tests` + `drift-and-ownership`, strict, enforce-admins, no required reviews, no force-push/deletion. That is recorded as an observation under FZ-07, but the row's disposition is the maintainer's to change.\n- No invented conclusions for B2–B7; no decision D1–D3 pre-empted; ADR-KERNEL-07 D-4 strict xfail untouched.\n- Credential hygiene is deliberately **not** mentioned in this public repo's docs.\n\n### Evidence\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| allowlist entries before vs after | **34 / 34, identical sequence and bytes**; `parse_allowlist` sets equal; file CR-free and ASCII |\n| `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` diff shape | 3 hunks, **0 deletions**: sync line inserted, DEBT-031 one pure insertion, 27-line section inserted |\n| every SHA cited in the new text | resolves to a commit in `main`'s history (`ecddbff`, `9b172d0`, `e1293f4`, `0ff0937`, `80a1bb8`, `1a09941`, `c4d62b3`, `e438387`, `7cefd6d`) |\n| test counts cited (21 / 35 / 67) | match `--collect-only` on the merged tree; B1 test list and B8 events/defaults checked against the code |\n| new table | 9 rows, 5 cells each (no stray `|`) |\n| claims about open items | FZ-01/02/05/06 re-checked on `e438387` by inspection (K4.2 `wf_result.output or \"\"`; `except Exception` in-band error token; `ModelRouterAdapter` `success=True` with no read of `execution_detail`; `ExecutionRegistry` has only `create/get/ids`; 16 `_emit_event` sites, 1 mentions `execution_id`) |\n| `scripts/check_drift.py` | 15/15 PASS (DRIFT-13 reads `KNOWN_ISSUES.md`) |\n| full suite, local | on the merged tree `5e173d4`, system Python 3.12: **1967 passed, 1 xfailed**, 0 failed (this PR adds no tests: its diff is two documentation files). The count is higher than the 1904 I measured before the merge because `main` gained tests via #56 in between. With a venv interpreter 8 `tests/core/sandbox/test_namespace_backend.py` tests fail (`execvp` ENOENT inside the sandbox chroot); the same 14 tests pass with the system interpreter — environmental (known tooling trap), not a product failure |\n| new gate on this run's real pytest output | passes |\n\n### Review notes — a correction I owe you\nWhile proofreading the R-1 text I found that my PR #55 wording overstated the protection: \"the new gate closes the old masking path\". Probed with real pytest: it **does** go red when ≥2 failing ids collapse to one truncated prefix, and when the real id is listed — but a **hand-truncated** entry (`tests/x.py::test_p[a`) **can still tolerate a single failing ` - ` id** (1 failed, entry listed → gate passes). R-1 in the register states exactly that, and the list header says not to write such an entry. No current entry is affected (0 of 34 contain ` - `). The fix (bracket-aware split) remains a separate, reviewed follow-up.\n\n### Update after opening: `main` moved, conflict resolved by a merge commit\nWhile this PR waited, `main` advanced from `e438387` to `7464a84` (PR #56, the `/import` boundary fix, and the documentation PRs #58, #48 and #49; none touches a file or symbol cited here: orchestrator, model_router, registry, resilience, scheduler, event_stream, ci_test_gate, ci.yml). The PR became `dirty` with **one** conflict: the top-of-file `Last synchronized` chain in `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` (main added its own Oct 5 line above the same Sept 16 entry). I merged `main` into this branch (merge commit `5e173d4`, parents `bdbe51a` + `7464a84`; no rebase, no force-push) and kept all three lines byte-identical to their sources, newest first: this PR's line, main's Oct 5 CodeQL line, main's already-prefixed Sept 16 line. Re-verified on the merged tree: diff vs `main` is still exactly the two files (+45/−5); the 34 allowlist entries are identical to `main`'s; `check_drift.py` 15/15 PASS.\n\n### CI result (real GitHub runners)\n| head | tests | drift-and-ownership | CodeQL | Analyze (python / actions) | Graphify |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `5e173d4` (current head) | success | success | success | success / success | no new run (Graphify reviews a PR once, on its first head) |\n| `bdbe51a` (superseded by the merge) | success | success | success | success / success | neutral (\"No PR-changed functions were verified\"; no findings, no review comments) |\n\n**Runner pytest summary — still awaiting the maintainer's log confirmation (I cannot read runner logs).** Because `main` gained tests, the number is no longer `1890`. My *derived, unverified* expectation: local 1967 − the 14 tests the runner skips (the same offset as before: local 1904 vs runner 1890 + 14 skipped) = **`1953 passed, 14 skipped, 1 xfailed`**, which should equal the number in `main`'s own post-merge run for `7464a84`. Gate step: `pytest exit code: 0` / `Test gate passed`.\n\n### Merge gate\n`tests` and `drift-and-ownership` green on the head; runner summary equal to `main`'s at `7464a84` (expected `1953 passed, 14 skipped, 1 xfailed`, derived — to be confirmed by the maintainer from the log) and gate line `pytest exit code: 0` / `Test gate passed`; allowlist entry diff empty (re-checkable; prints nothing when only comment lines changed: `git diff origin/main -- docs/architecture/D10_KNOWN_ENVIRONMENTAL_FAILURES.txt | grep -E '^[+-]' | grep -vE '^(\\+\\+\\+|---)' | grep -vE '^[+-]#'`; a negative control with an appended entry prints that entry); branch contains `main` (`7464a84`); no force-push. **Not merged without the maintainer's go-ahead.**\n\nContent commit: `bdbe51a`; head: `5e173d4` (merge of `main` `7464a84`). Rollback: revert this PR's merge commit.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Q9gxgWEp4VAGfNHHQDfuz1\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
