    "body": "## B9 — FZ-07: the `tests` gate must not pass on errors, empty runs or a lost exit code\n\n### Defect (FZ-07)\nThe `tests` job ran `pytest ... | tee ... || true` and then gated only on `^FAILED ` lines that are not in `docs/architecture/D10_KNOWN_ENVIRONMENTAL_FAILURES.txt`. pytest's exit code was thrown away, so anything that does not print a `FAILED` line was invisible to the gate: collection errors, fixture/setup/teardown errors, `INTERNALERROR`, a run that collected nothing, a killed or truncated run, pytest never starting.\n\nReproduced against the **real workflow text** (the two `run:` blocks executed verbatim under `bash -e`, GitHub's default shell, with a fake `pytest`): **15 of 24 scenarios were wrongly green** on `main` (`80a1bb8`).\n\n### Fix\n- `scripts/ci_test_gate.py` (new, stdlib only, unit-tested) makes the decision. The workflow records pytest's real exit code (`PIPESTATUS[0]`, since `tee` would hide it) and calls the script.\n- The gate passes **only if** all of these hold:\n  1. exit code is `0`, or `1` with every failure already listed (`2` interrupted/collection, `3` internal, `4` usage, `5` nothing collected, and `127/130/137/139/…` crashes or kills are failures by themselves; a missing or garbled exit-code record is a failure);\n  2. the final pytest summary line is present (a truncated run has none);\n  3. no `ERROR <path>` / `INTERNALERROR` entries, no `error` in the summary, and at least one passed test;\n  4. exit `0` has no `FAILED` lines; exit `1` has distinct `FAILED` node IDs equal to the summary's `N failed`, and every one is in the known-failure list.\n- The test step still never fails by itself (as before); the gate step is what turns the job red. Check names (`tests`, `drift-and-ownership`) are unchanged, so branch protection is unaffected. The exit-code file is uploaded with the pytest output for auditing.\n\n### Non-goals (explicitly NOT in this PR)\n- **The known-failure list is not touched** (zero diff to `D10_KNOWN_ENVIRONMENTAL_FAILURES.txt`): not widened, not pruned, not re-classified. Matching semantics are preserved exactly (exact node ID, `#`/blank lines ignored, an entry that no longer fails is fine, a CR-bearing ID still cannot match).\n- ADR-KERNEL-07 D-4 strict xfail untouched (it stays `1 xfailed`).\n- No change to `drift-and-ownership`, `release.yml`, dependency pins, or any product code.\n- The tracked-file mutation by the test suite (`config/*.toml`, `data/context.sqlite`) is a separate issue and is not pulled in.\n\n### Evidence (local, sandbox, Python 3.12)\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| 24-scenario matrix over the workflow's real `run:` blocks, **old gate** (`80a1bb8`) | 9/24 correct, **15 wrong** (all the holes above) |\n| same matrix, **new gate** (`7cefd6d`) | **24/24 correct** |\n| gate vs **real pytest 9.1.1 output**, 12 situations (pass, fail, fixture error, teardown error, collection error, nothing collected, strict XPASS, all skipped, logged `ERROR`, warnings, failure+error, xfail) | all classified correctly; pytest exit codes observed 0/1/2/5 as assumed |\n| listed failure through the gate (real pytest output) | tolerated; same failure + a setup error → red; captured-log `ERROR    x:file.py:4 …` lines do **not** trip it |\n| `tests/test_ci_test_gate.py` | **67 passed** (decision matrix, CLI contract, real-workflow wiring) |\n| mutation check (26 mutants of the script and of `ci.yml`: ignore exit code, drop each check, allowlist widened, `\\|\\| true` re-added, `PIPESTATUS[1]`, exit-code record removed, gate step swallowed, wrong list …) | **26/26 killed**; 2 initial survivors were weak tests, fixed |\n| flakiness of the new module | 12/12 sequential, 6/6 parallel |\n| full suite, local | **1904 passed, 1 xfailed**, exit 0 (= 1837 + 67 new) |\n| real full-suite output through the new gate | passes (exit 0, 1904 passed) |\n| `scripts/check_drift.py` | 15/15 PASS |\n| script on Python 3.11 / 3.13 | passes the real output; exit-code-2 case is red |\n\n### Review notes (PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS §18.3)\n- **Architectural impact:** CI gate only. **Governance:** strengthens it (assurance layer upstream of the runtime, DEBT-033 class); no runtime authority changes. **Replay/observability:** the gate prints exit code, summary line, known failures seen, and each failure reason; the exit-code file is an uploaded artifact.\n- **Risk:** this is the first time the stricter gate runs on a real runner. If `tests` goes red here it is a **finding that was previously masked, not a gate bug to be papered over**; the answer is to fix or explicitly classify the cause, never to widen the gate.\n- **Residual / not claimed:** the \"HF connectivity\" label on the 34 listed tests is still unverified as a cause. For information only: the maintainer-read runner summary for `main` showed `1788 passed, 14 skipped, 1 xfailed` with no failures, i.e. none of the listed tests failed on that run. Whether to prune the list is a separate decision (B10/D-item), not made here. The header comment of the list file still says only `FAILED` lines fail the build; that wording is now slightly stale and is left for B10 so this PR keeps a zero diff on that file.\n- **Rollback:** revert the single commit.\n\n### CI result (real GitHub runners, head `7cefd6d`)\n| head | tests | drift-and-ownership | CodeQL | Analyze (python / actions) | Graphify |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `7cefd6d` | ✅ (all steps incl. **\"Gate on pytest exit code, errors and unlisted failures\" = success**) | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ / ✅ | ✅ gate PASS (\"worth a look\"), 1 advisory (dispositioned below) |\n\nThis is the first run of the stricter gate on a real runner: it passed, so on this run pytest's exit code was recorded as `0` (or `1` with only listed failures), a summary line was present, there were no errors and at least one test passed. Step conclusions are read from the Actions API; **I cannot read the runner log itself** (log hosts are blocked from the session), so the exact pytest counts are still for the maintainer to confirm:\n\n**Runner log, confirmed by the maintainer:** \"Run test suite\" step ends with `1890 passed, 14 skipped, 1 xfailed, 2 warnings`; the gate step output was confirmed correct (`pytest exit code: 0`, `Test gate passed`).\n\n**Correction of my earlier expectation (my arithmetic error, not a CI discrepancy):** this PR body first said `1855 passed`. That used `main`'s old count of 1788 and forgot that `main` (`80a1bb8`) already contains B8's +35 tests. Correct chain on the runner: `a21711e` 1788 → B8 head `0ff0937` **1823** (maintainer-read; `80a1bb8`'s tree is byte-identical to `0ff0937`, tree `a4af0644…`) → this PR **1890 = 1823 + 67**. The 67 new tests all ran (skipped stays 14, xfailed stays 1). Local cross-check: 1837 → 1904 = +67.\n**Warnings:** the 67 new tests emit none (module run with `-W error`: clean). The local run shows 1 warning (a Starlette/`httpx` deprecation in `tests/test_audit_fixes.py`); the runner's count of 2 comes from its own dependency set and is not attributable to this PR. Warnings do not affect the gate (exit code 0). The `main` post-merge log line (`1823 passed, 14 skipped, 1 xfailed, N warnings`) is where to compare N.\n\n### Review dispositions (Graphify; advisory, marked \"NOT verified\" by the bot — probed against the code)\n1. **\"FAILED node IDs containing ' - ' are truncated before allowlist matching\" (`scripts/ci_test_gate.py:114`)** — **VERIFIED as behaviour, INHERITED, not introduced here, and fails closed.** The old shell did `sed 's/ - .*//'`; the script keeps it on purpose (allowlist semantics unchanged, pinned by `test_allowlist_semantics_unchanged`). Probe with real pytest (`test_p[a - b]`, `test_p[a - c]` both failing):\n   - **old gate:** listing the truncated prefix `tests/test_x.py::test_p[a` turns **both** failures green (false-green path); listing the full IDs is red;\n   - **new gate:** red in both cases — the summary says 2 failed but only 1 distinct truncated ID exists, which the new count check rejects. So the new gate **closes** the old masking path instead of widening it;\n   - the remaining defect is a false **red**: a legitimately listed failure with ` - ` in its parametrize id cannot be tolerated by writing its real ID. **No current entry is affected (0 of the 34 contain ` - `).**\n   - **Disposition: residual, not fixed here.** Changing the parse is a small bracket-aware split, but it alters allowlist matching and Graphify does not re-review follow-up pushes. Tracked for B10 / a follow-up; maintainer may ask for it in this PR.\n2. **Risky pattern `no-stderr-to-stdout` on `pytest ... 2>&1 | tee`** — **not a defect, unchanged behaviour:** the run step has always merged stderr into the captured log; the gate needs both streams in one file.\n3. **Risky pattern: `GATE ERROR` printed to stdout** — **by design:** the gate's whole report goes to one stream (Actions merges both); the exit code (2) is what fails CI.\n4. **\"Docs that may be stale\" (`CURRENT_STATE.md`, `KNOWN_ISSUES.md`, `K2_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md`, …)** — matches on the generic symbol names `run` / `fail` / `evaluate`; none describe this gate. The real doc work (register FZ-07, refresh the stale wording in the list's header) is B10 after implementation is evidenced.\n\n### Merge gate (what must be true before this merges)\n`tests` and `drift-and-ownership` green on the PR head (**met on `7cefd6d`**; CodeQL/Analyze/Graphify also green); runner pytest summary `1890 passed, 14 skipped, 1 xfailed` (= 1823 + 67; **confirmed**) and a gate-step line `pytest exit code: 0` (**confirmed**) from the runner's own log (a green check alone is not enough evidence for a gate PR); branch up to date with `main` (`80a1bb8`); PR tree == `7cefd6d` only; no force-push or history rewrite. **Go-ahead given by the maintainer after the log confirmation.**\n\nCommit: `7cefd6d`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Q9gxgWEp4VAGfNHHQDfuz1\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
