  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/53",
    "id": 4731183515,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABGgAhmw",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/53",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/53.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/53.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/53",
    "number": 53,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "fix(learning): contain background-job failures so they cannot kill the web server (B8 / FZ-03)",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "## B8 — FZ-03: background-job failures must not kill the web server\n\n**Scope:** `learning/scheduler.py`, `core/event_bus.py` (3 event names), and one new test module. Nothing else. FZ-01/02/04/05/06/07 and the ADR-KERNEL-07 D-4 strict xfail are untouched.\n\n### Defect (FZ-03)\n`Scheduler._loop_crawler` / `_loop_cleaner` ran their lazy imports (and every loop parsed its interval) **outside** their `try/except`. An `ImportError` escaped `Scheduler.start()`'s `asyncio.gather` and `main.py`'s `asyncio.gather(server.serve(), scheduler.start())`, ending the process and the healthy web server with it. `stop()` only flipped a flag, so multi-hour sleeps were never interrupted; failures were `print()`ed.\n\n### Fix\n- **Every job tick is guarded** (lazy imports, config reads, the work). A failure is logged server-side with traceback under an opaque `error_ref` (`core/error_ref.py`), counted, announced on the bus, and retried at the job's **normal cadence**. It never disables the job, so it recovers by itself once the cause is fixed.\n- **Cleaner preflight:** the cleaner historically imported its module at loop start (process start). That import is kept, now guarded, so a missing dependency is reported at once (`phase=\"preflight\"`) rather than hours later.\n- **Supervisor:** a loop that crashes outright is restarted with exponential backoff, at most `max_restarts` (5) per sliding `restart_window_s` (600 s); beyond that the job is **abandoned** (critical log + event). `start()` never raises for a job fault; only cancellation propagates.\n- **Intervals:** unusable config falls back to the job default; every interval is floored at `min_interval_s` (60 s) so a bad value cannot create a hot loop.\n- **Shutdown:** `stop()` wakes sleeping loops at once; cancelling `start()` leaves no child running; a second `start()` while running raises instead of doubling the loops.\n- **Observability:** `logging` (traceback server-side), bus events `learning.job_failed` / `learning.job_recovered` / `learning.job_abandoned` (added to `EVENTS`), and read-only `Scheduler.status()`. Events and `status()` carry **job name, exception class name and `error_ref` only — never exception text**, because `GET /events` streams every catalogued event to unauthenticated clients (DEBT-025; DEBT-037 convention).\n- `_training_cycle` / `_distillation_cycle` / `_gap_detection_cycle` / `trigger_module` are **byte-identical** to `main`. Historical cadence and run order preserved.\n\n### Non-goals (explicitly NOT in this PR)\n- `cleaner.run_all` is synchronous and still blocks the event loop while it runs (separate finding).\n- Tracked-file mutation by the test suite (`config/*.toml`, `data/context.sqlite`) — separate hygiene issue; these files are not in this diff.\n- `main.py`, `interface/api.py`, crawler/cleaner internals, the per-module `print()` handlers inside the cycle methods.\n- No FZ-01/02/05/06/07 work; no CI/allowlist change.\n\n### Evidence (local, sandbox, Python 3.12)\n| | pre-fix (`a21711e`) | fixed |\n|---|---|---|\n| poisoned `cleaner` import, real default intervals, `main.py` gather shape | `gather` **raised** `ModuleNotFoundError` at startup | survives; failure observed in `status()` |\n| poisoned `crawler` import | `gather` **raised** at startup | survives; failure observed |\n\n- **Tests:** 35 new in `tests/test_scheduler_failure_containment.py` — the mission's ten scenarios, in `main.py`'s exact gather shape with a fake server and real `sys.modules` import poisoning; plus interval handling, event catalogue, bus-failure and gate behaviour.\n- **Mutation check:** 13 injected defects (unguarded tick, unguarded supervisor, `stop()` not waking sleepers, unguarded emit, exception text in events, floor removed, gate removed, window never forgets, unbounded restarts, double start, preflight removed, no recovery event, `config.get` errors uncaught) — **13/13 killed**.\n- **Flakiness:** 30/30 isolated, 10/10 under 4-way CPU contention.\n- **Full suite:** `main` 1802 passed / 1 xfailed → B8 **1836 passed / 1 xfailed** (+34 = new tests; the xfail is the strict ADR-KERNEL-07 D-4 one); with `0ff0937`: 1837 passed / 1 xfailed.\n- **Drift check:** 15/15 PASS.\n\n### Review notes (PROJECT_INSTRUCTIONS §18.3)\n- **Governance:** outside the Kernel boundary; no authority surface added. Failure reporting never raises into callers.\n- **Replay/observability:** new events are catalogued; payloads deliberately contain no exception text.\n- **Security:** no exposure of exception detail to `/events` clients; behaviour of the sandbox/authz paths unchanged.\n- **Compatibility:** `Scheduler.__init__` gains keyword-only args with defaults; `start()`/`stop()` signatures unchanged. **Behaviour change:** intervals below 60 s are raised to 60 s (shipped defaults are ≥ 1 h).\n- **Rollback:** revert the single commit.\n\n### CI result (real GitHub runners)\n| head | tests | drift-and-ownership | CodeQL | Analyze (python / actions) | Graphify |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `e1293f4` | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ / ✅ | ✅ gate PASS, 4 advisories (dispositioned below) |\n| `0ff0937` (current) | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ / ✅ | **not run** on this push (accepted evidence exception, see Merge gate). Observed on PR #51 and #53: Graphify reviews a PR once, on the first head it sees, and did not run on any follow-up head; its docs do not describe a re-run trigger. All its findings are dispositioned below. |\n\n**Runner pytest summaries** (read from the Actions logs by the maintainer; I cannot read them — the log hosts are blocked by the session's egress policy):\n- `main` `a21711e`: **1788 passed, 14 skipped, 1 xfailed**\n- B8 `e1293f4`: **1822 passed, 14 skipped, 1 xfailed** → exactly **+34 passed**, skipped/xfailed unchanged\n- B8 `0ff0937`: **1823 passed, 14 skipped, 1 xfailed** → exactly **+35 passed** vs `main`, skipped/xfailed unchanged (confirmed by the maintainer from the runner log; includes the new race test 9d)\n(Local sandbox runs show 1802 → 1836 → 1837 with no skips; the environments differ, so the runner-to-runner delta is the authoritative one.)\n\n### Review dispositions (Graphify advisory review; all four marked \"NOT verified\" by the bot — each probed against the code)\n1. **\"Distillation job no longer honors `learning.training_enabled`\"** — **DISPROVEN.** The gate reads the setting on every tick: 0 distillation runs while disabled, runs resume after enabling at runtime (probe + `test_distiller_gate_skips_without_counting_as_success_or_failure`; mutant \"gate removed\" is killed).\n2. **\"Child task cancellation is swallowed by `start()`\"** — **DISPROVEN for `start()`**: cancelling `start()` raises `CancelledError` and all children are done (`test_9b`). **Nuance, accepted:** cancelling a *single* child from outside stops only that job (`status()` shows `stopped`, no restart, no event); `start()` and the other jobs continue. Nothing in the codebase cancels these tasks.\n3. **\"Crawl completion event can turn a successful crawl into a failed job\"** — **DISPROVEN.** `bus.emit` isolates subscriber errors (`core/event_bus.py`): a raising `learning.crawl_done` subscriber leaves the crawler at 0 failures (probe). The original code also emitted inside its `try`, so this is not a regression.\n4. **\"Stale `start()` cleanup can clobber a newer scheduler run\"** — **VERIFIED and FIXED in `0ff0937`.** If a second `start()` began in the loop turn between the last child finishing and the first `start()` resuming, the first call's `finally` reset `_running` and dropped the newer run's tasks, ending it at once. Narrow (needs a contrived interleaving; production calls `start()` once from `main.py`), but a real lifecycle bug. Fix: cleanup runs only if the call still owns `self._tasks` (4 production lines). `test_9d` builds the interleaving deterministically and fails without the guard (mutant killed); 0/25 flaky runs; local full suite 1837 passed / 1 xfailed.\n\n### Merge gate (what must be true before this merges)\n`tests`, `drift-and-ownership`, CodeQL, Analyze green on the PR head (Graphify: accepted evidence exception, below); the scheduler tests (35) and the **+35 runner delta** (1788 → 1823 passed, skipped/xfailed unchanged) confirmed from the **runner's own pytest output** (the `tests` job swallows pytest's exit code, see FZ-07, so a green check alone is not enough); branch up to date with `main`; PR tree == `e1293f4` + only the `0ff0937` guard commit; no force-push or history rewrite.\n\n**Graphify gate exception (accepted evidence exception, recorded by the maintainer):** Graphify ran successfully against e1293f4. Three advisories were disproven; the fourth identified the stale start() cleanup race, which is fixed by 0ff0937 with a regression test. Graphify provides no documented/manual rerun mechanism and historically does not rerun on follow-up pushes. Therefore the prior Graphify result is accepted for this PR, with the final-head race fix independently verified by the test suite.\n\nThis is **not** \"Graphify green on `0ff0937`\": Graphify did not run on `0ff0937`. The only relevant advisory (#4) was fixed by `0ff0937` and is covered by `test_9d` plus the runner's +35 delta.\n\nCommits: `e1293f4` (B8 fix + tests) → `0ff0937` (start() identity guard, review follow-up). Pushed as a fast-forward; no force-push, no history rewrite; branch up to date with `main` (`a21711e`).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01Q9gxgWEp4VAGfNHHQDfuz1\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
