    "body": "Documentation only. No code, test, config or contract change.\n\n## Problem\nADR-KERNEL-04's Sept 13 addendum, `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` (DEBT-020) and `CURRENT_STATE.md` state that `fix/debt-020-completion-semantics-sep2026` was kept (\"left on its own branch\", \"not deleted\"). That ref no longer exists on `origin`. When and how it was deleted is recorded as **UNKNOWN**.\n\n## Change (3 files, +15 / -1)\n- `ADR_KERNEL_04_FALSE_COMPLETION_FIX.md`: new dated addendum (Oct 2, 2026) with the correction.\n- `KNOWN_ISSUES.md`: one addendum paragraph in the DEBT-020 entry.\n- `CURRENT_STATE.md`: new top \"Last synchronized\" line; the previous top entry is prefixed \"Prior sync\".\n\nThe original Sept 13-14 statements are left in place as the historical record.\n\n## Evidence\n- The work is not lost: 3 commits (`a5883fc`, `809fa53`, `fcd3700`; merge-base `f7058d3`) remain at `refs/pull/16/head` (PR #16, CLOSED, unmerged).\n- They are now also preserved at `archive/fix-debt-020-completion-semantics-sep2026` (tip `fcd3700`); `git ls-remote` confirms the tip equals PR #16's head.\n\n## Not changed\nDEBT-020 stays closed. ADR-KERNEL-04's decision (main's implementation is canonical) and the freeze verdict are unchanged.\n\n## Verification\n- `scripts/check_drift.py`: 15/15 pass before and after the edit; `git diff --check` clean.\n- Branch is 1 ahead / 6 behind `main`. Dry-run merge into current `main` is clean; `main`'s concurrent `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` edit (DEBT-021/DEBT-039 table rows) is in a different region from this change.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-10-03T21:26:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-03T21:36:27Z",
