  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/50",
    "id": 4728833755,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABGdxG2w",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/50",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/50.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/50.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/50",
    "number": 50,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "test: net_proxy - read the response to EOF instead of assuming one recv() is a whole response",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "## What\n\nFixes the receive assumption in two tests of `tests/core/sandbox/test_net_proxy.py`. **Test file only; the proxy is unchanged.** Independent hygiene: not part of the network redesign and not on the redesign branch.\n\n- `test_plain_http_to_allowed_host_is_forwarded` and `test_connect_to_allowed_host_tunnels_real_data` asserted on a single `recv(4096)`. The upstream writes headers and body separately and the proxy relays each chunk as it arrives, so one `recv()` can return only the headers. A failing run captured `resp = b'HTTP/1.0 200 OK\\r\\n...Content-Length: 2\\r\\n\\r\\n'`.\n- Both tests now read until the peer closes (the proxy relays the upstream's close), bounded by the socket's 3 s timeout. Other tests keep their single-`recv` helper.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Standalone file, before: **19 of 30 runs failed** (16 `plain_http`, 3 `connect`). After: **0 of 60**.\n- Mutation check: a proxy that drops the last byte of each relayed chunk fails both fixed tests, so they still detect real data loss. The proxy was restored byte-identical.\n- `tests/core/sandbox`: 147 passed, twice, with Docker up. mypy clean on the file. 0 containers, 0 endpoints, 0 temp dirs afterwards.\n- The proxy itself lost no data (read-to-EOF complete in 300 of 300 warm and 20 of 20 cold requests; see the network-redesign study, finding F11).\n\n## Base\n\n`sandbox-fabric` (`1b829fc`), **not `main`**: `_net_proxy.py` and its test exist only on `sandbox-fabric`. This PR targets `sandbox-fabric`.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-10-03T18:41:42Z",
