    },
    "body": "## What\n\nRegisters **DEBT-041**: `DockerBackend` sandbox containers run as uid 0 with Docker's default capability set, including `NET_RAW`, because `_build_create_args` has no `--cap-drop`. `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` only, one row added.\n\nThis is finding **F9** of the `sandbox-fabric` network-redesign study, tracked as a **hardening item separate from the redesign**. It is a prerequisite for the redesign only if the chosen design relies on caller identity (option O2). Spoofing via `NET_RAW` was **not** tested; the row says so.\n\n## Scope\n\n- One file, one row added, after DEBT-039. Based on `main` at `69df55f`. No code, test or capability change.\n- Priority is deliberately left \"Not yet triaged — to be set in review\".\n\n## Note for merging\n\nA sibling PR registers **DEBT-040** (finding F6) with an insertion at the same spot. Whichever merges second needs its branch updated, with a trivial conflict in `KNOWN_ISSUES.md`. The ids are fixed by the rows themselves, so if this one merges first, DEBT-041 will sit before DEBT-040 until the other lands.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-10-03T18:33:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-05T10:20:47Z",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-05T10:20:47Z",
    "merged_at": "2026-10-05T10:20:47Z",
