    },
    "body": "## What\n\nRegisters **DEBT-040**: a networked `DockerBackend` sandbox can reach host services bound to `0.0.0.0` (or the bridge address) through the network gateway. `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` only, one row added.\n\nThis is finding **F6** of the `sandbox-fabric` network-redesign study. It is **separate from DEBT-039** (sibling-proxy reachability) and DEBT-039's row is not changed. The user ruled that F6 is within checklist item C2 and must be closed before `NETWORK_ALLOWLIST` can be re-supported.\n\n## Added after opening\n\nA scratch probe against the unmodified `NamespaceBackend` (on `main`, which claims `NETWORK_ALLOWLIST`) shows the same behavior, so the row now covers both backends. Observed once on one host; `NamespaceBackend` is otherwise not audited. This widens DEBT-040's exposure beyond `DockerBackend`, where the claim is already withdrawn.\n\n## Scope\n\n- One file, one row added, after DEBT-039. Based on `main` at `69df55f`. No code, test or capability change.\n- Priority is deliberately left \"Not yet triaged — to be set in review\".\n- The study document it cites lives on branch `study/sandbox-network-redesign`, not on `main`; it is referenced by path and branch, as DEBT-021 and DEBT-039 reference `sandbox-fabric`.\n\n## Note for merging\n\nA sibling PR registers **DEBT-041** (finding F9) with an insertion at the same spot. Whichever merges second needs its branch updated, with a trivial conflict in `KNOWN_ISSUES.md`.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-10-03T18:33:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-05T10:15:52Z",
