    "body": "## What\n\nDocumentation follow-up to the `sandbox-fabric` reconciliation closure (Stage 5, Result 2). `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` only.\n\n- **Register DEBT-039** (Security): cross-sandbox egress via a sibling's proxy in `DockerBackend` (checklist item C2 = FAIL). The id is confirmed; DEBT-038 is the `/distill` `module_name` traversal already on `main`. **Priority is deliberately left \"Not yet triaged — to be set in review.\"** The network redesign is future work, not opened.\n- **Update DEBT-021**: a Docker-backed implementation exists on the `sandbox-fabric` branch (not on `main`) and is **explicitly incomplete** per `docs/architecture/sandbox-execution-fabric-existing-code-reconciliation.md` §19.4 (`sandbox-fabric` commit `a574091`): 22 of 28 checklist items PASS; A1, A9, C2, C3, D9 open; B4 an accepted exception for `handoff.md` only. The debt stays open; priority Low is unchanged.\n\n## Scope\n\n- One file: `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` (1 line replaced, 1 line added).\n- Based on `main` at `4ab5345`. No `sandbox-fabric` code, tests or docs are included, and `docker_backend.py` is not on this branch.\n- The §19.4 document this refers to lives on `sandbox-fabric`, not on `main`; the references are by path and commit, as in the existing DEBT-021 row.\n\n## Review points\n\n- DEBT-039 priority/impact wording is a proposal for the reviewer to set.\n- DEBT-021's impact cell now warns not to rely on `DockerBackend` for network-allowlist or isolation guarantees (withdrawn; DEBT-039) or for the A9/C3 socket-family protections (unverified/blocked).\n",
    "created_at": "2026-10-03T01:12:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-03T01:16:40Z",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-03T01:16:40Z",
