  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/46",
    "id": 4713849102,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABGPehDg",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/46",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/46.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/46.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/46",
    "number": 46,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "fix: route every module-name filesystem path through core/module_paths.module_child() (containment invariant)",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "Separate from #43 (docs, merged) and #44 (`/import` root). Behavior-preserving for every legitimate name; one stated behavior change below.\n\n**Problem.** A module name became a filesystem path in ~20 places by joining it onto a root (`DATA_RAW / module_name`, `EVAL_DIR / f\"{module_name}.json\"`, ...), each relying on its caller having validated it. `.isidentifier()` at the entry points (factory, export/import, `/distill`) is a naming rule; CodeQL does not treat it as a filesystem barrier, and `/train` is guarded by registry membership, not by an identifier check.\n\n**Change.**\n- New `core/module_paths.py`: `module_child(root, name, suffix=\"\")` requires the name to be one path component and the `resolve()`d result (symlinks followed) to be `is_relative_to(root)`. Fixed error text (`InvalidModuleName`, a `ValueError`); the input is never echoed. The code-controlled suffix is inside the contained path, so it cannot be used to climb out.\n- Applied at every sink: `core/brain_export.py` (export: `mod_dir`, output path, eval, raw; import: `mod_dir`, eval dest), `core/module_factory.py`, `core/module_registry.reload_module`, `learning/{trainer,cleaner,crawler,evaluator,gap_detector,finetuner,distiller}`. `crawler.run_module` validates before it reads config.\n- **Preserved on purpose:** the existing `.isidentifier()` checks stay as the naming rule and are not weakened; `/train`'s registry-membership guard is untouched; and `module_child` is wider than `.isidentifier()` on what a name may be, so a registry directory such as `my-module` keeps working (there is a round-trip test).\n\n**Behavior change.** A module directory that is itself a symlink pointing outside its root is now rejected (export/import/reload/fine-tune). Symlinks *below* the module directory are not inspected. `learning/finetuner.py` gains a module-level `MODULES_DIR` constant (instead of an inline `Path(__file__)` expression) so it can be tested.\n\n**Tests.** `tests/test_module_name_containment.py`, 76 tests: helper accept/reject, suffix, symlink out/in, root-as-child; 13 sink functions x 4 hostile names asserting `InvalidModuleName` and an unchanged directory tree; crawler rejects before touching config; distiller sink; `reload_module`; round-trip for `my-module`; export and import refuse a symlinked module dir (decoy survives).\n- Against `main`'s unfixed sink sources (plus only the patchable `MODULES_DIR` constant in finetuner, so it fails on behavior rather than a missing attribute): **51 fail / 25 pass**. The 25 are the helper's own unit tests, the `my-module` round-trip, and the distiller tests (already guarded by #37), which pass either way by design.\n- Full suite on this branch: **1727 passed, 1 xfailed, 0 failed.** This run had `chromadb==0.5.3` installed, so the 8 tests the previous session recorded as \"environmental\" ran and passed.\n- Trial-merged with #44: no conflicts, **1743 passed, 1 xfailed**. (`brain_export.py` is touched by both in different hunks.)\n\n**Not claimed.** I can't run CodeQL here: whether `resolve()` + `is_relative_to()` inside a helper clears the remaining `py/path-injection` alerts is untested, so none are dismissed and they stay open until the next analysis. `/train` and the other HTTP routes still do their own earlier checks; this PR adds the sink-side invariant, it does not replace them. Not touched: `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` / `CURRENT_STATE.md` (a docs follow-up after both PRs merge). The checks are not atomic with the later file operations (a directory swapped between check and use). `.isidentifier()`-style import-path concerns in `reload_module` (`importlib` name) are unchanged.\n\nNot merged.",
    "created_at": "2026-10-02T07:28:31Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-04T00:43:53Z",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-04T00:43:53Z",
