    "body": "## Live draft-plan check: runbook, the first valid result (llama3, n=11), and corrections — docs + tests only\n\n**Not for merging until reviewed.** This PR does **not** enable the proposed feature: `creative_content_anchor_enabled` stays `false` by default. Merging it would not accept ADR-KERNEL-07 (still PROPOSED), and green CI establishes repository correctness, not architectural acceptance. The behavioral choice (options A–D in the result record) is still open.\n\n### Files\n1. `docs/studies/OCBRAIN_LIVE_CHECK_DRAFT_PLAN_RUNBOOK_OCT2026.md` — how to run the check in a Codespace; evidence-validity checker; troubleshooting\n2. `docs/studies/OCBRAIN_LIVE_CHECK_DRAFT_PLAN_RESULT_OCT2026.md` — the evidence record (new)\n3. ADR-KERNEL-07 + `ADR_INDEX.md` — §10.4 UNKNOWN → **OBSERVED for one model**; corrected descriptions (verbatim D-5 text untouched)\n4. `scripts/live_check_draft_plan.py` — **docstring only** (AST-identical code)\n5. `tests/test_live_check_runbook_validator.py` — executes the validator **extracted from the runbook itself**\n\n### Result (llama3 via Ollama, 11 requests, one run — **model identity recovered after the fact: `llama3:latest`, 8.0B, Q4_0, ID `365c0bd3c000`; sampling uncontrolled (the code sets no temperature or seed), so a re-run is expected to differ**; see the record's limits)\nAll 11 plans multi-step (median 7, 83 steps, **0 single-step**); **no step names a concrete subject/genre/premise**; most are generic authoring workflow, a minority presuppose form/process (character profiles, thesis + sources, \"beta readers\"…). Neither useful context nor premise speculation, cleanly. **Two separate conclusions:** the single-step hypothesis is refuted; whether the observed behavior is undesirable is *not* established by this run. The harness's `speculative` label was **saturated (11/11)** and is not evidence. **No containment applied; options A–D are in the record; disposition is Moncif's.**\n\n### My errors, corrected here\n- The runbook validator treated \"interpretation == request\" as a failure sign. `description` **is** the raw request by design (`intent.py:1090`); the old validator would have rejected this valid run. Fixed, with a regression test (and a one-bad-row test found by mutation).\n- The ADR hypothesis (single-step plans; input = \"the interpretation, not the raw request\") was wrong on both counts.\n- The Option C response's \"interpreted intent\" line is an **echo of the request**; ADR §2/§9 corrected.\n- \"Touches no memory\" in the harness docs was false (creates empty `.data/memory/*.db`); corrected earlier in this PR.\n\n### Also found, not fixed (separate workstreams)\n`_fts_escape()` fails on 9/14 realistic queries (documented only for `?`); the clarification response joins steps as `story.; 2.` and its example text is story-specific for every artifact kind.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-10-02T01:12:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-14T21:38:39Z",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-14T21:38:39Z",
