    "body": "Separate from the docs/register and shared-validation work. Behavior change on both `/import` routes.\n\n**Problem.** `POST /import` (`interface/api.py`) and `POST /brain/v2/import` (`core/brain_api.py`) pass a caller-named server-side `bundle_path` straight to `import_module()`, which opened it as a zip. These are the two `py/path-injection` source groups the register classifies as \"by design\" (CTX-EXPORT-001's open design question).\n\n**Change.**\n- `core/brain_export.py`: `import_root()` and `resolve_bundle_path()`. The path is canonicalized with `resolve()` (symlinks followed) and must satisfy `is_relative_to(import_root())`. `import_module()` calls it before touching the file, so the sink enforces it for every caller. Containment is checked before existence, so there is no probe for files outside the root.\n- Import root = `global.import_root` in `settings.toml` (documented, commented out). **Unset = `data/exports`**, where `export_module()` writes, so export -> import still round-trips with no config. Relative setting is resolved against the project root. A relative `bundle_path` is taken relative to the root.\n- Both handlers return `400` with a fixed message that echoes neither the input nor the root.\n\n**Decisions I made that you may want to change** (small edits): (1) default root is `data/exports` rather than \"refuse until configured\"; (2) relative `bundle_path` means relative to the root, not to the process CWD; (3) no `.ocbrain` suffix requirement.\n\n**Existing tests changed on purpose (3, in `tests/test_brain_export_security.py`).** They kept their bundles outside the new root. Their root is redirected to `tmp_path` so they still exercise what they were written for, and the end-to-end zip test now uses `match=\"resolves outside\"` because `BundlePathError` is a `ValueError` and the old bare `pytest.raises(ValueError)` would have passed for the wrong reason.\n\n**Tests.** `tests/test_import_root_containment.py`, 16 tests: inside (absolute/relative), outside, `..` x3, prefix-sharing sibling, symlink escape, NUL byte, configured root replaces default, relative configured root, sink rejects before opening the zip, no existence oracle, missing-in-root stays FileNotFound, both routes -> 400 with fixed text.\n- Against `main`'s unfixed source files: **15 of 16 fail**; the one that passes (missing bundle inside root -> `FileNotFoundError`) passes either way by design. Several of the 15 fail on `AttributeError` for the new helper rather than on behavior; the handler and sink tests are the behavioral ones.\n- Full suite on this branch: **8 failed / 1647 passed / 1 xfailed**. The 8 are the known chromadb-not-installed failures (`TestA7SystemController` x6, `test_module_factory_security` x2); the 4 break/system_ctrl files are ignored, as before.\n\n**Not claimed.** I can't run CodeQL here, so whether it accepts `resolve()` + `is_relative_to()` as a barrier for the `/import` alerts is untested; those alerts stay open until the next analysis shows otherwise. Not fixed: the checks are not atomic with the later `ZipFile` open (a file swapped inside the root between the two). Not touched: `KNOWN_ISSUES.md`/`CURRENT_STATE.md` (CTX-EXPORT-001 status needs a docs follow-up after this merges), and no signature/checksum on bundles, which remains the larger CTX-EXPORT-001 question.\n\nNot merged.",
    "created_at": "2026-10-02T00:47:33Z",
