    "body": "Docs only: `KNOWN_ISSUES.md`, two table rows, no new ID.\n\n**DEBT-037** -- its \"same class, not fixed\" sentences were stale. Now records that answer text (#39, `1a1621a`), the updater `check_error` (#40, `9b172d0`) and the factory duplicate-module path (#42, `4bb5974`) are fixed and merged, that four existing tests were changed on purpose in #39 (config errors such as \"No adapter_runtime or model_router configured\" are no longer visible in the reply), and what was deliberately left alone (event payloads, `WorkerResult.error`, tracing spans; `PlannerWorker`'s `WorkerResult.error` reach untraced). I folded these into the existing entry instead of opening new IDs; if you want one or three separate entries, say so and I'll split them.\n\n**DEBT-038** -- adds the per-route classification of CodeQL's `py/path-injection` sources, re-derived from SARIF analysis `1878148129` on `9b172d0` (30 results, 8 HTTP sources in `interface/api.py` and `core/brain_api.py`): `/modules/new` and `/train` guarded, both `/distill` routes fixed, both `/export` routes fixed, both `/import` routes by design (CTX-EXPORT-001's no-signature question). Open alerts on `main`: 32 (29 path-injection + 3 test-file url-substring); the 1-result difference vs. the analysis is unexplained.\n\n**Correction to the session handoff:** it said CodeQL lists no sources in `core/brain_api.py`. The latest analysis does (lines 130, 146, 152); the classification is unchanged.\n\nNot changed: alert dispositions, `/import` behavior, `_safe_extractall`, Dependabot/chromadb. Those need your call.\n\nChecked: both rows still have 6 `|`; `git diff` is exactly 2 lines; file is LF-only (no CRLF churn). Not merged.",
    "created_at": "2026-10-02T00:35:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-02T00:43:16Z",
