  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/42",
    "id": 4708075682,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABGJ-Iog",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/42",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/42.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/42.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/42",
    "number": 42,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "Fix: drop the absolute install path from the duplicate-module error (/modules/new 400 body)",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "## What\n\n`core/module_factory.create()` raised `ValueError(f\"Module '{name}' already exists at {dest}\")`, and `POST /modules/new` returns `str(e)` as the 400 detail -- so the response carried the **absolute install path** of the modules directory. CodeQL does not flag it.\n\nReachable only when the factory has been deliberately re-enabled (`global.module_factory_enabled`; disabled by default as the RCE-001 containment, DEBT-021), so **low severity**. Fixed because it is the same class as the other response-text leaks (#34 / #36 / #39 / #40) and the message loses nothing by dropping the path.\n\n## Fix\n\nMessage is now `Module '<name>' already exists.` The one existing test on it matches `\"already exists\"`, which still holds.\n\n## Tests -- `tests/test_module_factory_error_disclosure.py` (2)\n\n`create()` and the real `/modules/new` handler, against a temp modules dir. **Both fail against the unfixed `module_factory.py`** and pass with the fix.\n\n## Not in this PR\n\nRegister entries for #39 / #40 / this PR (deliberately deferred -- sibling PRs would conflict on the same table lines; to be added in one docs PR after they land).\n\n## Verification\n\nFull suite on current `main` (`ecddbff`): 8 failed / 1628 passed / 1 xfailed -- the same `chromadb`-unavailable 8; the xfail comes from the merged ADR work, not this change. Reverted the usual `config/*.toml` + `data/context.sqlite` test-run pollution.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-10-01T18:46:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-02T00:02:54Z",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-02T00:02:54Z",
