    "body": "## ADR-KERNEL-07 — creative content-anchor detector, slice 1 (PROPOSED, **flag OFF**)\n\n**A narrow experimental detector — not intent sufficiency.** It flags one class of under-specification (a form-only creative request such as \"write a 1000 words story\") and asks a specific question instead of generating. It reads request text only and cannot see that \"write a 1000-word science-fiction story\" is still under-specified (pinned as executable known-limit tests).\n\n### Architecture (D-5 decided by Moncif: Option C)\n`interpret_request → detect (pure, non-governing) → plan → compile() → EXISTING OrchestrationGovernor at Plan Compilation → ESCALATE → question + interpreted plan`\n- **No new gate, no new governance boundary, no new governance evaluation** (tested: the sequence of governance evaluations is identical with the flag on and off). K4.2's \"no dedicated clarification gate\" is preserved; DRIFT-10 untouched.\n- The one contract touch: an additive, keyword-only, default-`None` `content_anchor` argument on `compile()`. With the flag off, `handle()` and the `compile()` call are unchanged.\n- The detector module imports no governance code (AST-tested). Out-of-scope requests **abstain** (never \"sufficient\").\n\n### Behavior\n`[runtime] creative_content_anchor_enabled = false` by default → **merging changes no behavior.**\n\n### Status — please read\n- **Merging is not acceptance of the ADR.** ADR-KERNEL-07 stays **PROPOSED**. D-1/D-2 are PROPOSED, D-3/D-4 DEFERRED (own ADR for session identity; Test D stays a strict `xfail`); explicit acceptance is Moncif's.\n- **Live draft-plan behavior is UNKNOWN** (needs a configured model provider). `scripts/live_check_draft_plan.py` is the instrument; no containment (`plan_steps=[]`) is applied. Run it before the flag is ever enabled.\n- Slice 1 is **detect → ask → stop**; there is no cross-turn lifecycle.\n\n### Files (12)\n`core/cognitive/content_anchor.py` (new) · `core/cognitive/compiler.py` · `core/governance/orchestration_governor.py` · `core/orchestrator.py` · `main.py` · `config/settings.toml` · ADR + index row · the study (unmodified) · `scripts/live_check_draft_plan.py` · 2 test files. **No Constitution, CURRENT_STATE, KNOWN_ISSUES, ROADMAP, or drift-rule changes.**\n\n### Verification (local, on the merge commit)\n75 new detector/compile/orchestrator tests + 17 harness tests (+92 vs main); existing `test_compiler.py` unchanged (42 pass); 9 + 4 mutation checks red as intended; `check_drift.py` 15/15; reconciliation audit 16/16 (negative control confirmed it can fail); 0-conflict merge with main@2e5cfc0. In my sandbox the failing-ID set is identical to main's; CI is the real gate.\n",
