  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/40",
    "id": 4695221793,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABF9tmIQ",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/40",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/40.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/40.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/40",
    "number": 40,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "Fix: stop returning raw exception text in the update-check result (/updates, /update/install)",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "## What\n\n`interface/updater.check()` put exception text into `UpdateResult.check_error`: `f\"Could not reach GitHub: {e}\"` for `requests` failures -- whose messages carry the connection target (proxy host/port, resolver errors, URLs) -- and `str(e)` for anything else. `GET /updates` returns `check_error` verbatim and `POST /update/install` returns it as `error`, so an API caller saw that text.\n\nCodeQL does **not** flag it. It was listed in DEBT-037 as \"same class, different feature area, not fixed\"; fixed here on its own.\n\n## Fix\n\nBoth branches log the exception (message + traceback) under a fresh uuid and set `check_error` to `\"<prefix>: <ExceptionClass> (ref <uuid>)\"`. The helper is **file-local** (`_log_and_ref`) instead of importing `core/error_ref.py`, so this PR stands alone on `main` and does not depend on #39; unify later if both land.\n\nThe CLI (`interface/cli.py`) prints `check_error` from `/updates` to the local console; it needs no change and now shows the class and ref.\n\n## Tests -- `tests/test_updater_error_disclosure.py` (3)\n\nThe requests-failure branch, the generic branch, and the real `/updates` and `/update/install` handlers. **All three fail against the unfixed `updater.py`** and pass with the fix.\n\n## Not in this PR\n\n- Register entry: deliberately not here (sibling PRs would conflict on the same table lines); to follow once these land.\n- `core/module_factory.py`'s `\"already exists at {dest}\"` message (returned via `HTTPException(400, str(e))` from `/modules/new`, puts the absolute install path in a 400) -- noted, not changed.\n\n## Verification\n\nFull suite: 1,534 passed / 8 failed (same `chromadb`-unavailable baseline, +3 new tests). Branched from `main` at `2e5cfc0`. Reverted the usual `config/*.toml` + `data/context.sqlite` test-run pollution.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-09-30T19:44:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-02T00:07:08Z",
