  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/39",
    "id": 4695194646,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABF9r8Fg",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/39",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/39.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/39.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/39",
    "number": 39,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "Fix: stop returning raw exception text in caller-visible answers ([Error in <module>: ...])",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "## What\n\n`merger.merge()` appends error results to the string a caller receives, and `Orchestrator`, `PlannerWorker` and `core/dispatcher.py` built those results from `f\"[Error in {mod}: {exc}]\"`. So whatever a module's exception said -- host, URL, filesystem path, config value -- was returned to `/query` clients.\n\nCodeQL does **not** flag this (no request-to-response taint path; it goes through `gather(return_exceptions=True)` and an f-string). It was found by grepping for exception text formatted into strings after the CodeQL-flagged sites were fixed in #34/#36, and was listed as real-but-unfixed in the earlier write-up. Verified real: `merger.merge()` explicitly appends error answers to the returned string.\n\n## Fix\n\nNew `core/error_ref.py::log_and_ref()` logs the exception with its traceback under a fresh uuid and returns the id. Each site now answers `[Error in <module>: <ExceptionClass> (ref <uuid>)]`. Module name and exception class stay because they make the entry actionable (same convention as `/debug` in #36); the message goes to the log under the same ref.\n\nSites: `core/orchestrator.py`, `core/workers/planner.py`, `core/dispatcher.py`. The dispatcher is **dormant** (nothing imports it); changed anyway because it built the same string. `interface/api.py::_log_and_redact` and `core/brain_api.py` keep their own equivalents -- not refactored here.\n\n## Decision for you: four existing tests changed on purpose\n\nThese asserted the raw message was **in the answer**: `test_planner_worker::test_module_dispatch_exception_contained`, `test_planner_capability_migration::test_capability_failure_folded_into_merged_error_like_legacy` and `::test_no_adapter_runtime_and_no_model_router_is_contained_not_raised`, `test_k2_2_runtime_migration::test_workflow_failure_returns_error_not_crash`.\n\nThe property they protect -- the failure is **contained and folded into the answer, never raised** -- is unchanged and still asserted. What changed: the message is now asserted to be in the server log under the answer's ref and **not** in the answer. So this is a design choice, not only a bug fix: config errors like `No adapter_runtime or model_router available` are no longer visible in the reply, only in the log. If you prefer the old visibility for our own controlled messages, the alternative is a dedicated \"safe to show\" exception class -- a bigger change I did not make.\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test_answer_error_disclosure.py` (3): the helper; the real `Orchestrator.handle()` call site; the dormant dispatcher. Run against the **unfixed** `core/` files: 6 fail (the orchestrator and dispatcher tests plus the four updated ones), helper test passes either way.\n\n## Not covered\n\n- `WorkerResult.error` / event-payload `\"error\": str(e)` fields (internal channels, not answer text) and `PlannerWorker`'s `\"pipeline error: {e}\"` `WorkerResult.error` -- whether it reaches a caller is untraced.\n- `interface/updater.py` `check_error` -- separate PR.\n- Register entry: deliberately not in this PR, to avoid conflicts between sibling PRs; to follow once these land.\n\n## Verification\n\nFull suite: 1,534 passed / 8 failed (same `chromadb`-unavailable baseline, +3 new tests). Reverted the usual `config/*.toml` + `data/context.sqlite` test-run pollution. `feature/intent-sufficiency-slice1` also edits `core/orchestrator.py`, but in different hunks (76-129, 304-316 vs ~744).\n",
    "created_at": "2026-09-30T19:41:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-10-01T09:14:50Z",
