  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/37",
    "id": 4677096772,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABFsbVRA",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/37",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/37.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/37.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/37",
    "number": 37,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "Fix: validate module_name on both /distill routes (path traversal into data/raw)",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "## What\n\nTwo HTTP routes take `module_name` in the request body and pass it, unvalidated, to `learning/distiller.py`, where `_save_pairs` does `(DATA_RAW / module_name).mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)` and writes `distil_*.json` under it:\n\n- `POST /distill` (`interface/api.py`)\n- `POST /brain/v2/distill` (`core/brain_api.py`, router prefix `/brain/v2`)\n\n## Reproduced before fixing (real handlers, unfixed source)\n\n- Ollama unreachable, zero pairs generated, `module_name=\"../../created_by_request\"`: a directory is still created **outside** `data/raw` (the `mkdir` runs before the pair loop).\n- `POST /brain/v2/distill` with a traversal name: **HTTP 200** and a directory created outside `data/raw`.\n- When the model returns parseable pairs it also writes `distil_<hash>.json` there.\n\n## Impact, as far as I demonstrated it\n\nAttacker-controlled **directory creation plus a constrained JSON write**. Not \"arbitrary file write\": filenames and extension are fixed, contents are model output seeded by the caller-supplied `topic`, and I did not show overwrite of an existing file or code execution. Reachability is the loopback listener plus the CSRF header, which is not authentication (DEBT-025). Suggested severity from review: P2 / Medium -- **your call**, not recorded as decided.\n\n## How it was found\n\nBy asking CodeQL where its remaining `py/path-injection` flows start (SARIF code flows), instead of assuming they were `.isidentifier()` false positives. They start at HTTP handler parameters. `/train/{module_name}` is guarded by an `in _orchestrator.modules` allowlist (registry keys are directory basenames, `module_registry.py:48`, so that is a valid path boundary), `/modules/new` by `factory_create`'s `.isidentifier()` check. `/distill` had neither. The second route was missed on my first pass and surfaced while checking an outside review's claim that it existed.\n\n## Fix\n\nSame `.isidentifier()` convention as `module_factory.create()` and `brain_export.py`. `_require_module_identifier()` runs at the top of `distill_topic` (before any model call) and inside `_save_pairs`, so every caller of the sink is covered. Both handlers return **400** with a fixed message (no echo of the input); before the second handler guard, `/brain/v2/distill` already blocked the traversal via the sink guard but answered with an unhandled 500. Keep both layers: the sink guard is the invariant for other callers.\n\nThe invalid field is `module_name`; `topic` is free text and deliberately unconstrained.\n\n## Tests -- `tests/test_distill_module_name.py`, 5 tests\n\nThe four traversal tests (sink, `distill_topic` before any network call, both handlers) **fail against unfixed source** and pass with the fix; the `/brain/v2` test also fails against sink-guard-only source (`500 != 400`). The legitimate-name test passes on both by design.\n\n## Not in this PR\n\n- `CURRENT_STATE.md`: not updated -- it has no bounded row for this finding.\n\n## Register (added after #36 merged)\n\n`KNOWN_ISSUES.md` **DEBT-038**: one finding with two affected entry points (`POST /distill`, `POST /brain/v2/distill`), **Medium (P2)**, worded as out-of-root directory creation plus constrained JSON artifact creation -- not arbitrary file write. Records that `module_name` is the validated field and `topic` is free text, and lists the other `learning/*` alerts as unclassified. Note: the ID is `DEBT-038` (next free; `DEBT-038`/`039` appear nowhere else on `main` or in any open PR), whereas the request said `DEBT-039` -- renumber if that was intentional.\n\nBranch was merged with `main` (`a949b8d`, includes #36) with no conflicts; full suite on the merged tree: 1,531 passed / 8 failed (same `chromadb` baseline).\n- Other `learning/*` `py/path-injection` alerts: `trainer` is reachable only via `/train` (allowlist-guarded). `crawler` / `cleaner` / `gap_detector` are said to iterate registry keys -- **not traced by me**, so not classified here.\n- `core/orchestrator.py` / `core/workers/planner.py` `[Error in ...]` answer text (see #36).\n\n## Verification\n\nFull suite: 1,529 passed / 8 failed, the same `chromadb`-unavailable baseline. Reverted the usual `config/*.toml` + `data/context.sqlite` test-run pollution before committing. Branched from `main` at `2520cb4`.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-09-29T12:23:04Z",
