  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/36",
    "id": 4670295658,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABFl8Oag",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/36",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/36.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/36.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/36",
    "number": 36,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "Fix: close the two stack-trace flows #34 missed (model_router error token, /debug) + correct the zip-slip claim",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "## Why this exists\n\nAfter #34 merged, CodeQL's `py/stack-trace-exposure` alerts at `interface/api.py`'s `StreamingResponse` sink and `/debug`'s `return report` stayed open. The alerts' own SARIF code flows show why: exception text reached those sinks by two routes #34 didn't touch.\n\n## Fixes (commit 9631e4e)\n\n1. **`core/model_router.py::_ollama_stream`** yielded `f\"[Error: {e}]\"` as an ordinary stream token. `_stream_response` forwards every token verbatim, so transport errors (host/URL detail) reached the SSE client in-band. Now logs the exception with `exc_info` under an `error_id` and yields `[Error: model request failed (ref <id>)]` -- same `[Error: ...]` shape.\n2. **`interface/api.py` `/debug`** returned `str(e)` for module-health and Ollama-connectivity failures. Now returns the exception class name + an `error_id`, full detail in the server log. **Behavior change to look at in review:** `/debug` is a diagnostics endpoint, so it now shows the class name instead of the message.\n\nTests: 2 more in `tests/test_api_error_disclosure.py`. Each was run against the pre-fix source and **fails there**, passes on the fix (I did not do that check for the first batch of tests in #34).\n\nDocs: `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` / `CURRENT_STATE.md` still said the #34 work was \"not yet on main\" -- corrected. DEBT-037 now records that #34 left these flows open. Also softened an overstatement in the CTX-EXPORT-001 addendum and the `export_module()` comment: the traversal exposed `*.json` files and fixed-name subpaths (`weights/active`, `knowledge.db`) plus an `output_path` escape, not \"arbitrary directories\".\n\n## Correction of #35 (commit e2fd5a0, comment-only)\n\n#35 described `import_module()`'s `zf.extractall()` as an exploitable arbitrary file write and \"more severe\" than the export-side finding. **That was wrong.** CPython's `zipfile` drops `..`, `.`, empty and drive/absolute components from member names (`ZipFile._extract_member`). Checked on Python 3.12.3: plain `extractall()` on `../`, nested `../` and absolute-path members left nothing outside the destination. CodeQL flags the call, but there was no exploitable write.\n\n`_safe_extractall` is still harmless and slightly stricter (rejects the whole bundle instead of silently rewriting names), so I did not revert it. This commit only fixes its docstring and the test-class docstring. Keep vs. revert is your call; #35 also didn't reduce the CodeQL count meaningfully (35 -> 34 open, and it still flags the `extractall()` inside the helper).\n\n## Not fixed\n\n- `core/orchestrator.py` and `core/workers/planner.py` build `f\"[Error in {mod_name}: {res}]\"` answers from per-module exceptions, which reach the caller as answer text. Same class, not CodeQL-flagged.\n- The ~30 `py/path-injection` alerts remain open; CodeQL's flow runs past the `.isidentifier()` guards, so they are scanner findings awaiting a disposition, not evidence the guards fail.\n\n## Verification\n\nFull suite: 1,526 passed / 8 failed (same `chromadb`-unavailable baseline). Reverted the usual `config/*.toml` + `data/context.sqlite` test-run pollution before committing.\n",
