  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/35",
    "id": 4657781509,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABFaAbBQ",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/35",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/35.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/35.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/35",
    "number": 35,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "Fix: reject path-traversal zip members in import_module() (zip-slip, CodeQL py/path-injection)",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "## Summary\n\nFound while checking the repo's full open Code Scanning alert list after merging #34 -- not named in the write-up that prompted that PR, and more severe than what it described (arbitrary write, not read).\n\n`import_module()`'s `zf.extractall(tmp_path)` extracted an attacker-supplied `.ocbrain` bundle with no per-member path validation. `zipfile.extractall()` strips leading slashes/drive letters on its own (a stdlib protection against the absolute-path variant) but does nothing about relative traversal -- a bundle containing an entry named e.g. `\"../../etc/cron.d/evil\"` could write outside the extraction directory, before `manifest.json` (and the `module_name` validation #34 added downstream of it) is even read.\n\n**Fix:** new `_safe_extractall()` helper -- resolves every member's target path against `dest` and refuses the whole archive if any member would land outside it (fail-closed: validates all members before extracting any of them, so a traversal entry can't be smuggled past review by pairing it with an otherwise well-formed `manifest.json` in the same zip). `import_module()` now calls this instead of `zf.extractall()` directly.\n\n## Explicitly not handled here\n\n- Symlink members whose *target* (not path) escapes `dest` -- a narrower, separate concern from the path-traversal-on-extraction issue CodeQL flagged.\n- Zip-bomb / decompression-size limits -- a different hardening category from path injection, left for its own disposition.\n\n## Tests\n\n`tests/test_brain_export_security.py::TestZipSlipExtraction` -- 3 tests: malicious entry rejected before `manifest.json` is read (proven fail-closed and against a decoy); legitimate bundles still extract normally; the real `import_module()` call site rejects a malicious bundle end-to-end, not just the helper in isolation.\n\n## Verification\n\nFull suite re-run: **1,524 passed / 8 failed**, same pre-existing `chromadb`-unavailable baseline every recent sync in this project hits. Zero regressions. Reverted the same incidental `config/*.toml` + `data/context.sqlite` test-run pollution as #34's branch, same reason (pre-existing test-isolation gap, unrelated).\n\nBranched from `main` post-merge (`bd290ff`, includes #34) rather than off the now-closed #34 branch.\n",
