  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/34",
    "id": 4650226554,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABFSzTeg",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/34",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/34.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/34.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/34",
    "number": 34,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "Fix: close export-side CTX-EXPORT-001 path injection + redact API exception detail (CWE-209/497)",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "## Summary\n\nTwo CodeQL findings against live `main`, both re-verified by direct code reading rather than accepted from the report alone.\n\n### 1. `core/brain_export.py` -- path injection (CTX-EXPORT-001, `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` DEBT-019)\n\n`export_module()` never received the `.isidentifier()` validation `import_module()` got in the Sept 15 fix -- confirmed the two functions diverged, not assumed from prior notes. `module_name` reaches this function unvalidated from an HTTP request body (both `interface/api.py`'s and `core/brain_api.py`'s `/export` routers call the same function) and was used to build `mod_dir`, `weights_src`, `kb_src`, `eval_src`, `raw_dir`, and `output_path`. A `module_name` like `\"../../etc\"` let export read, and hand back inside the returned bundle, arbitrary directories outside `modules/`; a name containing `/` could also steer `output_path` outside `EXPORTS` via pathlib's `/` operator.\n\n**Fix:** the same `.isidentifier()` check `import_module()` / `module_factory.create()` already use, applied before `mod_dir` is built. Same convention, not a new one.\n\n### 2. `interface/api.py` + `core/brain_api.py` -- exception detail exposed to clients (new DEBT-029)\n\n`POST /query` returned `f\"{type(e).__name__}: {e}\"` as `error`, plus a full traceback in `meta` when `global.debug` was set. Reading the flagged code surfaced two more instances of the identical pattern in `interface/api.py`'s `_stream_response` (both single- and multi-module streaming paths) -- not named by CodeQL, same file. `core/brain_api.py`'s `_stream_query` (CodeQL-flagged) has the same pattern.\n\n**Fix:** `interface/api.py` gets a shared `_log_and_redact()` helper (3 call sites); `core/brain_api.py` gets a file-local equivalent (1 call site, kept local rather than importing across the interface/core boundary for one helper). Each logs the real exception + traceback server-side via `exc_info`, and returns/yields only `{\"error\": \"internal_error\", \"error_id\": <uuid>}` to the caller.\n\n## Explicitly out of scope (flagged, not fixed here)\n\n- `interface/updater.py`'s `check()` (`/updates`, `/update/install`) has the identical `check_error=str(e)` pattern -- different feature area, left for its own disposition.\n- `learning/*.py` (`cleaner.py`, `crawler.py`, `distiller.py`, `gap_detector.py`, `trainer.py`) builds several paths from `module_name` with no `.isidentifier()` guard -- confirmed present, not confirmed exploitable (registry-sourced; `config.py`'s registration path not traced far enough to be sure). Candidate for its own audit pass.\n- Signature/checksum/content validation on import bundles, and CTX-EXPORT-001's Kernel v1.0 freeze classification -- both unchanged, both remain Moncif's call.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `tests/test_brain_export_security.py::TestExportModuleNameValidation` -- 2 new tests (traversal rejected before any filesystem access, proven against a decoy; legitimate names still pass through to the pre-existing not-found check).\n- `tests/test_api_error_disclosure.py` -- new file, 4 tests (the redaction helper directly, `POST /query`, `_stream_response`'s single-module path, `core/brain_api.py`'s `_stream_query`). The multi-module streaming path shares the tested helper and yield shape but wasn't separately integration-tested.\n\n## Verification\n\nFull suite re-run after the fix (light dependency set, `chromadb`/`sentence-transformers` not installed in this sandbox, matching this project's documented baseline): **1,521 passed / 8 failed**, all 8 the pre-existing `chromadb`-unavailable class (4 more files fail to even collect for the same reason, excluded, also pre-existing). Zero regressions. Confirmed no other `@app.`/`@router.` surface exists beyond these two files (repo-wide grep). Reverted incidental `config/*.toml` + `data/context.sqlite` changes made by running the suite against real fixtures instead of isolated ones -- pre-existing test-isolation gap, unrelated, not touched here.\n\n## Docs\n\nUpdated `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` (CTX-EXPORT-001 addendum + new DEBT-029 row) and `CURRENT_STATE.md` (CTX-EXPORT-001 summary row) -- the bounded, already-isolated cells only. The master \"Last synchronized\" narrative chains at the top of both files were deliberately not touched.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-09-26T22:51:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-28T10:55:11Z",
