    "title": "docs: restore CURRENT_STATE.md sync entry and fix table-row concatenation dropped during PR #23's merge race",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "PR #23 got merged (by 1h0lde4, via the branch) while a second, independent reconciliation of the same main-vs-branch conflict was still in progress on this branch -- a race, not a disagreement. Comparing the two resolutions after the fact found two small defects that made it into `main` at the merge point:\n\n1. **`CURRENT_STATE.md`**: the Sept 16-17 CTX-SCOPE-001 sync entry is missing from the chain entirely -- jumps straight from this branch's Sept 23 entry to the shared Sept 15 tail. The underlying facts still exist in `KNOWN_ISSUES.md`'s DEBT-019 row, so nothing was lost project-wide, but this file's own narrative chain has a gap.\n2. **`KNOWN_ISSUES.md`**: unrelated to (1) -- my own merge script (not `main`'s state) had briefly introduced a missing newline between the DEBT-019 and DEBT-021 table rows on this branch; caught and fixed before this push, confirmed absent from what actually merged into `main`, included here only because this branch is already ahead by that commit.\n\nDocumentation only. Zero code changes, zero test-file changes. Full suite re-confirmed on this exact diff: 1,515 passed / 8 failed (same pre-existing `chromadb`-unavailable set), zero regressions -- not that a 2-file prose diff could plausibly affect it, but checked rather than assumed.",
