    },
    "body": "Implements ADR-KERNEL-06's accepted mechanism plus its Sept 20 amendment (raw request as a citable source, deterministically verified against real assembled inputs, never trusted on say-so; selection gated on verified USER authority).\n\n**Closes CTX-AUTH-001b.** `TestCtxAuth001ParserAcceptance` reformulated per Moncif's Sept 20 instruction and passing.\n\n**Verified, not assumed:**\n- Full suite: 1,509 passed / 8 failed (same pre-existing chromadb-unavailable set). Zero regressions.\n- `live_citation_check.py` (Moncif's own adversarial harness), full default scale, `--dry-run obey-fabricate --fail-on-selected`: 30/30 benign requests verified-USER (100%); 90 exposed adversarial trials across all 3 payloads, 0 fabrications reached USER authority, 0 injected candidates selected, exit 0.\n- `--dry-run obey-honest`: every trial correctly capped at `cited_block_nonoperative`.\n\n**Not in ADR-KERNEL-06's original stated scope, flagged as it happened:** `core/memory/assembly.py` gained a new `assemble()` returning structured `Context` -- the existing `assemble_context()` only returns a flattened string, which cannot support per-block citation verification. Its own behavior and its other two callers (Orchestrator, PlannerWorker) are unchanged.\n\n**Freeze status:** narrows Kernel v1.0's NOT_FREEZE_READY verdict to REM-004 (whether the authority taxonomy/provenance model is sufficient as a general Kernel contract, a broader question this PR's runtime-behavior evidence does not settle) and CTX-EXPORT-001's freeze classification -- CTX-AUTH-001 (001a and 001b) is no longer a blocker.\n\nFull detail: `docs/architecture/decisions/ADR_KERNEL_06_VERIFIABLE_HYPOTHESIS_PROVENANCE.md` §8, `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` DEBT-019, `CURRENT_STATE.md`.\n\nOpened, not merged, from a Claude.ai chat session -- merge/branch-create happens via Claude Code or the GitHub web UI here, push had its own explicit one-time authorization; merge has not.",
    "created_at": "2026-09-23T19:09:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-23T21:59:17Z",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-23T21:59:17Z",
