  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/19",
    "id": 4581349352,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABERHX6A",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/19",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/19.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/19.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/19",
    "number": 19,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "fix(CTX-AUTH-001b): reconcile Sept 16 DEBT-019 patch; ADR-KERNEL-06 (design accepted, not implemented)",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "Reconciles the Sept 16 DEBT-019 / CTX-AUTH-001b patch against current `main` and lands the accepted design ADR.\n\n**This does not close CTX-AUTH-001b.** The ADR is Accepted, implementation is pending, and `TestCtxAuth001ParserAcceptance` stays intentionally red (it is also red on `main`).\n\n## What lands (9 files)\n- `docs/architecture/decisions/ADR_KERNEL_06_VERIFIABLE_HYPOTHESIS_PROVENANCE.md` + `ADR_INDEX.md`: Option A (source citation verified against the assembled `Context.blocks`), fail-closed, authority inherited never inferred. Numbered -06 (drafted as -05) because `ADR-KERNEL-05` is already held by the PROPOSED CTX-AUTH-001b deferral on `fix/ctx-auth-001-ctx-delete-001-sep2026`; the ADR carries a numbering note.\n- `core/memory/retrieval/context/context.py`, `builder.py`: `AuthorityLevel` enum (REM-004 groundwork) and `ProvenanceRecord.authority` (default `RETRIEVED`, fail-closed), assigned at the single production construction site. No runtime code reads `.authority` yet.\n- `core/cognitive/intent.py`: hardening only. Role-marker neutralization, an untrusted-context note on retrieved material, and output-shape containment (at most 5 candidates, non-increasing scores; drops are logged via `logger.warning`). Explicitly not authority-based acceptance.\n- Tests (`test_intent.py`, `test_intent_security.py`, `test_context_builder.py`) and the `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` CTX-AUTH-001 row.\n\n## Verification\n- Trial merge with `main` (`4669e21`): clean.\n- Touched test files: 137 passed / 1 failed (the intentional CTX-AUTH-001b marker).\n- The 11 test files importing the changed modules: `main` 417 passed / 1 failed; merged 425 passed / 1 failed. No regression.\n- Full suite not re-run in this pass (dependencies unavailable in the verification sandbox).\n\n## Impact\n- Governance: no governor or policy changes.\n- Replay / observability: no new events; the only new signal is the `logger.warning` above.\n- Persistence: none of the changed code touches persistence.\n- Behavior change to be aware of: `generate_hypotheses` now drops candidates beyond 5 or with out-of-order scores, and the context passed to the model is prefixed with an untrusted-material note.\n- Rollback: revert the merge commit.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-09-20T00:10:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-28T10:53:29Z",
