  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/16",
    "id": 4530566488,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABDgr1WA",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/16",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/16.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/16.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/16",
    "number": 16,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "[Superseded] DEBT-020 completion-gate redesign — do not merge",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "## Status: superseded, not merged\n\n`main` already has a working, tested, shipping implementation of DEBT-020's completion semantics (`b9948cd` / `docs/architecture/decisions/ADR_KERNEL_04_FALSE_COMPLETION_FIX.md`) — `Constraint.measure`/`comparator`/`target` + `is_satisfied_by()`, `WorkflowResult.constraint_violations`, and `Orchestrator.handle()` checking that before accepting a response as final.\n\nThis branch's own first commit is dated Sept 9, before that fix landed (Sept 10, 23:25) — its author was very likely unaware the problem had already been fixed by the time this branch's implementation commit landed (Sept 11, 06:19). It independently converged on nearly identical `Constraint` fields (same names, same `is_satisfied_by()` method) — but diverges completely downstream: a `CompletionStatus` enum + `completion_reason`, consumed by `EvaluatorWorker`, never integrated with what's already merged and live.\n\nConfirmed via an actual test-merge (not just inspection): 8 files conflict, 5 of them code (`core/cognitive/compiler.py`, `core/cognitive/planner.py`, `core/runtime/execution_outcome.py`, `core/workflow/definition.py`, `core/workflow/runtime.py`).\n\n**Explicit decision (Moncif, Sept 13, 2026):** main's implementation stays canonical. This does not reopen DEBT-020. `CompletionStatus`/`has_checkable_value()` are not being ported merely because they exist here — that would require a concrete architectural need and a fresh implementation against current `main`, not reconciliation of this stale branch.\n\nClosing without merging. The branch itself is left intact, not deleted, in case a later deliberate architecture review finds something specific worth extracting on its own merits.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-09-14T20:31:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-23T15:51:39Z",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-14T20:31:23Z",
    "merged_at": null,
