  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/14",
    "id": 4521379326,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABDX7F_g",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/14",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/14.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/14.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/14",
    "number": 14,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "Wire CTX-SCOPE-001 into its remaining live caller sites (+1 found in review)",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "## Summary\n\nCompletes CTX-SCOPE-001 (`docs/reports/context-compiler-remediation-register.md` REM-006), following on from PR #13. That PR landed the scope mechanism; this wires every live caller the closing audit named as unscoped, plus one it didn't.\n\n## What's wired\n\n| Site | What | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `core/workers/planner.py:218` | write (`_run()` step 8) | `scope = context.metadata.get(\"execution_id\", \"\")` — matches `core/workflow/runtime.py`'s own pattern, not a new convention |\n| `core/model_router.py:314` (`_build_prompt`) | read | The audit's own `\"planner.py:305\"` citation traces here, not to planner.py itself — both `_dispatch_module()` branches converge on this one sink. Threaded through 8 `ModelRouter` methods + `ModelRouterAdapter`'s capability payload, all defaulting to `\"\"` (unscoped/legacy) |\n| `interface/api.py:381` (`_save_context_background`) | write | `execution_id` added as a parameter |\n| `interface/api.py`'s direct `stream_route()` call | read | **Not in the original audit's list** — found during this pass's own verification. Bypasses `PlannerWorker` entirely (single-module streaming fast path) |\n\nDeliberately **not** touched: `core/workers/capability_executor.py:121`, which reaches the same `ModelRouter` chain with `context=\"\"` — safe today by accident (falsy-string guard short-circuits before `format_for_prompt()`), not by design, per the audit's own row #6. Not one of the named live sites; left as the pre-existing, tracked fragility it is.\n\n## Proof, not just \"doesn't crash\"\n\n- `tests/test_planner_worker.py::TestCtxScope001PlannerCallerWiring` — write side against a **real** `ContextMemory`, not a mock: two `PlannerWorker` runs with different `execution_id`s genuinely can't see each other's saved turns. Differential control confirms the no-`execution_id` legacy path still works unscoped.\n- `tests/test_model_router.py` — read side: `_build_prompt()`, `route()`, and `stream_route()` each asserted to forward the exact scope value to `format_for_prompt()`.\n- `tests/test_api_context_scope.py` (new file) — `_save_context_background` tested directly; `interface/api.py` had no test file before this.\n- 11 new tests total.\n\n## A mistake I caught before it landed\n\nApplying `core/orchestrator.py` as a straight file-level port (rather than a real merge) would have silently reverted main's independent Sept 6 DEBT-020 fix living in the same file. Caught by diffing the committed file against main before finalizing; fixed with an actual three-way merge. (This was in PR #13, surfacing it again here since it's directly relevant precedent for how this PR was built — same discipline applied throughout.)\n\n## Concurrent-session note\n\nMain moved substantially while this branch was in progress — another session (\"Watchdog-Reconciliation\") did its own merge of the branches this whole effort has been consolidating, then reconciled with PR #13 directly. Rebased cleanly (no conflicts on the code; one doc conflict resolved by combining both sync entries, newest on top). Also corrected one now-stale claim the rebase brought in: `CURRENT_STATE.md`'s \"Reconciled current state\" callout still asserted CTX-SCOPE-001 \"stays open\" with the three call sites unwired — struck through in place per this document's own convention, not silently rewritten, with a dated correction pointing to this work.\n\n## Tests\n\n1,474 passed / 15 failed / 4 errors. Fully explained: 1 pre-existing intentional CTX-AUTH-001 parser-acceptance red, 6 pre-existing chromadb-unavailable (this sandbox), 4 chromadb file-level errors (same), and 8 new failures in `tests/core/sandbox/test_namespace_backend.py` — confirmed identical on vanilla `origin/main` with no changes from this branch, environmental to this container (likely a custom venv path not resolving inside the namespace sandbox), unrelated to anything in this PR.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-09-13T23:05:48Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-28T10:52:49Z",
