    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/13",
    "number": 13,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "Selective port: CTX security fixes (CACHE-001, DELETE-001 resolved; AUTH-001, SCOPE-001 partially mitigated)",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "## Summary\n\nBranch-consolidation pass: selectively ports the real, tested fixes from `fix/context-security-findings-sep2026` — code and its paired test rewrite only, not that branch's stale `CURRENT_STATE.md`/`KNOWN_ISSUES.md` edits (17 commits behind current `main`). Documentation in this PR is freshly written against current `main` and the remediation register, reconciled empirically rather than accepting the source branch's own closing audit at face value.\n\n## What's resolved vs. what's not (verified by running the tests, not inferred)\n\n| Finding | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| CTX-CACHE-001 (REM-001) | **Resolved** | `TestCtxCache001Collision` now passes |\n| CTX-DELETE-001 (REM-007) | **Resolved** | `TestUnifiedMemoryDelete::test_delete_returns_false_when_l1_storage_deletion_fails` now passes |\n| CTX-AUTH-001 (REM-002) | **Partially mitigated, not closed** | Structural-containment half fixed (`TestCtxAuth001StructuralContainment` passes); parser-acceptance half untouched, still red (`TestCtxAuth001ParserAcceptance`). REM-002's own stated dependency on REM-004 (authority taxonomy) is unmet. |\n| CTX-SCOPE-001 (REM-006) | **Partially mitigated, not closed** | Mechanism built and tested (3/3 in rewritten `test_context_scope_security.py`), but 3 live call sites remain unwired: `core/workers/planner.py:218`, `:305`, `interface/api.py:381` (see `docs/Bugs Hunt & fix reports/CONTEXT_ISOLATION_CALLER_AUDIT_SEP2026.md`) |\n| CTX-EXPORT-001 (REM-008) | Untouched | Not in scope of the source branch |\n\nTwo things left as open questions for Moncif rather than decided in this PR:\n1. Whether CTX-AUTH-001's partial mitigation changes its priority pending Context Compiler's authority-taxonomy work (REM-004).\n2. Whether wiring the 3 remaining CTX-SCOPE-001 call sites should be prioritized now — that's new implementation, deliberately not done here.\n\n## Correction made during preparation\n\n`core/orchestrator.py` needed an actual three-way merge, not a file-level port — a straight port would have silently reverted main's independent Sept 6 DEBT-020 false-completion fix in the same file. Fixed via `git merge-file` against the real merge-base; both DEBT-020's 37 tests and the CTX-SCOPE-001 wiring are verified passing together.\n\n## Tests\n\n1,427 passed / 7 failed / 4 errors (from 1,422/11/4 on unmodified `main` at merge-base). All 4 errors and 6 of 7 failures are `chromadb` unavailable in the preparation sandbox (pre-existing, unrelated). The 1 remaining CTX-tagged failure (parser-acceptance) is intentional.\n\n## Commits\n\n1. Code + test rewrite + closing audit doc port (with the orchestrator.py 3-way merge)\n2. `CURRENT_STATE.md` / `KNOWN_ISSUES.md` / remediation register sync, rebased onto `main` after two concurrent commits (Sandbox-Fabric Phase 1 sync, C-MoE routing study) landed mid-session — both reconciled to preserve both sets of changes, not overwritten.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-09-12T22:25:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-13T23:13:35Z",
