  {
    "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pulls/12",
    "id": 4429580151,
    "node_id": "PR_kwDOSWs39c8AAAABCAYHdw",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/12",
    "diff_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/12.diff",
    "patch_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/pull/12.patch",
    "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/1h0lde4/ocbrain-v4.1/issues/12",
    "number": 12,
    "state": "closed",
    "locked": false,
    "title": "Two research reports: false-completion Kernel audit + C-MoE continuous-verification architecture proposal",
    "user": {
      "login": "1h0lde4",
      "id": 196927701,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOC7zg1Q",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/196927701?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/1h0lde4",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/following{/other_user}",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/gists{/gist_id}",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/events{/privacy}",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/1h0lde4/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "## What this is\nTwo investigation/research documents. No code changed, no tests added, no\nK-number assigned, no freeze blocker declared. Both reports route\nclassification decisions to project-owner review rather than deciding them.\n\n## 1. docs/Bugs Hunt & fix reports/FALSE_COMPLETION_KERNEL_AUDIT_PRE_IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT.md\nTraces the reported bug (10,000-word request -> 365 words claimed \"done\") to\na concrete, code-verified chain:\n- `core/workflow/runtime.py:280` sets workflow `success` from the last node's\n  mechanical success only (\"the call didn't error\")\n- Propagates unchanged through `:320` into `workflow.completed`, then into\n  `EvaluatorWorker.goal_completed` (`evaluator.py:172`)\n- `EvaluatorWorker` never reads `Constraint` at all, despite docs claiming it does\n- `FailureType.COMPLETED_WITH_PARTIAL_OUTPUT` exists but is never assigned;\n  the one place that reads it treats it as equal to `SUCCESS`\n- `validation_gate()` is real but is a memory-promotion gate, unrelated to\n  task-output scope -- naming collision with the pipeline the bug report assumed\n\nDoesn't map cleanly to K4.2, K4.3, or the Aug 27 watchdog work. New, unscoped\nterritory -- recommend routing to Moncif rather than assuming blocker status.\nThree items left OPEN: exact response-finalization location, `partial_output`\ncallers, resumability.\n\n## 2. docs/studies/OCBRAIN_CMOE_VERIFICATION_ARCHITECTURE_STUDY.md\nCompanion to the existing CMoE Cognitive Runtime Architecture Study. Finds no\nfrozen Verification/Critic/Evidence architecture exists in this repo (corrects\nthat premise -- same shape of error as the earlier \"K4.3 = C-MoE\" correction).\nWhat does exist: the CMoE study already reserved stub fields for verification\neverywhere (`verification_status`, a dedicated verification-confidence\ndimension, task-status capped at `COMPLETED_WITH_WARNINGS` until Verification\nexists) and explicitly deferred it as a future milestone.\n\nProposes an Evidence/Verification layer that:\n- Lives at the Kernel/execution layer, not inside C-MoE\n- Fills the existing stub fields rather than adding parallel ones\n- Reuses `EventStream.create_checkpoint()`/`replay()` (implemented, currently\n  unused -- DEBT-003) as the durability substrate\n- Escalates deterministic-first; cognitive PASS trusted less than deterministic\n  PASS (external research: LLM verifiers show a measured positive-label bias)\n\nPhased A/B/C/D recommendation at the end, flagged not decided.\n\n## Review needed\n- Does the false-completion finding get a K-number / DEBT entry, and does it\n  rise to a Kernel v1.0 freeze item?\n- Sign-off on the Evidence/Verification direction before any of it moves into\n  implementation.\n",
    "created_at": "2026-09-03T05:39:00Z",
